        openings: ("During a youth soccer game, {V} moved a chair {D} had left to hold a spot, and {D} walked over and shoved {V} backward over a cooler. {V} fell on an elbow and was left with a bruise and a scrape. Another parent filmed the shove at 10:15 and will tell you {V} never swung.", "{D} was already angry about a call, saw a chair moved, and walked over to ask why. {D} says {V} raised a hand in front of {D.his} face first. You will hear from the referee, who saw the push but not what came before."),
        closings: ("Both hands, a hard shove, a cooler, and a fall, on video. No swing from {V} appears anywhere on that recording. A chair is not a reason to put hands on another parent.", "{V}'s hand came up before the push, according to {D}, and the referee admits {V}'s hand moved near {D}'s face. The video begins only after the argument had started. The earlier minutes were never reviewed, and the doubt belongs to {D}."),
        timeline: [(0, "10 a.m.: the game begins."), (0, "10:10 a.m.: {V} moves the chair."), (0, "10:15 a.m.: {D} shoves {V}."), (1, "The league files its incident form.")],
