        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Friend's Jacket", "{DL} says the jacket was a friend's and {D.he} grabbed it by mistake."), E(.document, 1, "Photo of Jackets", "A photo of two similar jackets on the bench.")],
        role: "Sheriff's deputy",
        exam: [.direct("Why did you go to the park pavilion at 10:40 p.m.?", "\"A noise complaint. When I arrived, I smelled marijuana coming from a group of six people.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I searched a jacket on a bench and found two pre-rolled marijuana cigarettes in the pocket. A lab confirmed the material.\""), .direct("What did {D} say about the jacket?", "\"On my body camera, {D} says 'that's my jacket' and then says 'it's a friend's.'\""), .direct("What led you to the pavilion?", "\"A noise complaint around 10:30 about loud talking and music at the park. I arrived at 10:40 and smelled marijuana coming from the group.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I asked the group about it and searched a jacket sitting on the bench. In the pocket I found two pre-rolled marijuana cigarettes.\""), .direct("Whose jacket was it?", "\"{DL} said it was {D.his}, then said it belonged to a friend. The jacket held {DL}'s keys and wallet, which is why I cited {DL}.\""), .cross("{D} says the jacket was a friend's and was grabbed by mistake, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"That is what {D.he} says. The jacket on the bench was identical to a friend's.\""), .cross("Did {D} wear the jacket earlier?", "\"I understand {DL} wore it earlier. Several people sat near it.\""), .cross("There were two similar jackets on the bench, weren't there?", "\"Yes. A photo shows two jackets of the same make and color lying together on the bench.\""), .cross("Six people were in the group, weren't they?", "\"Yes. Nobody else claimed the jacket, though some of them smelled of smoke too.\""), .cross("The group had six people there, so you could not tell whose jacket it was from the bench alone, could you?", "\"Correct. That is why I asked, and why {D.he} was the one who said it was a jacket {D.he} owned.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Pavilion guest",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Whose jacket was on the bench?", "\"Mixed up. Two jackets looked the same, and people grabbed one or the other as the night went on.\""), .direct("Did {D} wear the jacket earlier that evening?", "\"Earlier, yes. {D} had it on at the start and then took it off when it warmed up.\""), .direct("Did anyone else sit near the bench?", "\"Several people. The bench was where we all left our things.\""), .direct("How do you know the defendant?", "\"We are good friends and were both at the pavilion that night. I brought the other jacket that was on the bench.\""), .direct("What did the jackets look like?", "\"Identical, the same brand and color. We bought them together at a sale last winter and often mix them up.\""), .direct("What did you see the defendant do with the jackets?", "\"Both were on the bench, and {D.he} picked one up when it got chilly. I did not see which one it was at the time.\""), .cross("Did you smell marijuana at the pavilion?", "\"Yes, I did. It came from the group. I could not say who.\""), .cross("Did you see anyone with pre-rolls?", "\"No. I did not see any.\""), .cross("Did the defendant say the jacket was {D.his}?", "\"I heard {D.him} say it was. Then {D.he} changed that.\""), .cross("Your jacket held nothing illegal, did it?", "\"No. Only my own things, a phone charger and a pair of gloves, and I told the deputy that.\""), .cross("You cannot say which jacket the defendant took, can you?", "\"No. They looked exactly the same, and it was dark under the pavilion lights.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} had marijuana in {D.his} jacket.", "{D} grabbed a friend's jacket by mistake."),
        allocution: "\"I made a bad choice, and I'm ready to deal with it.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had bought the pre-rolls that day.", "The friend's jacket was identical and was on the bench too."),
        defendant: [.direct("Whose jacket was the one on the bench?", "\"A friend's. It was identical to mine, and I grabbed it by mistake when the deputy asked.\""), .direct("Why did you say 'that's my jacket' first?", "\"I assumed it was mine. When I looked closer, I realized it was my friend's.\""), .direct("Did you know about the pre-rolls?", "\"No. I did not know they were in the pocket. I did not buy them.\""), .direct("What happened that night?", "\"We were at the pavilion for a friend's gathering. It got cold, so I picked up a jacket from the bench and put it on.\""), .direct("Why did you say it was yours?", "\"I thought it was mine, then realized it did not feel right in the pocket. I told the deputy it was probably a friend's.\""), .direct("What was in the pocket?", "\"My keys and my wallet. I had put them in earlier and did not check whether anything else was in there.\""), .cross("You are the only one who claimed the jacket, aren't you?", "\"I claimed it when I thought it was mine. I corrected myself right away.\""), .cross("The friend's jacket was identical. How can you prove that?", "\"I cannot. The friend can say. I know it sounds convenient.\""), .cross("You changed your answer on the body camera, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I said it was mine, and then said it was a friend's when the deputy showed me the pre-rolls.\""), .cross("You bought pre-rolls that day, didn't you?", "\"Yes, for a friend. I put them in a jacket pocket and did not mean to leave them where anyone could find them.\""), .cross("You said 'that's my jacket' before you said it was a friend's, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I was nervous and it came out wrong. I changed my answer when I saw what the deputy found.\"")],
        openings: ("A deputy answering a noise complaint at a park pavilion smelled marijuana from a group of six and found two pre-rolled marijuana cigarettes in a jacket on a bench. {D} was the only person who claimed the jacket.", "Weigh the defense proof, which will show that a friend's identical jacket was on the bench, that {D} grabbed the wrong one, and that {D} never knew what was in the pocket."),
        closings: ("Two pre-rolls in a jacket {D} said was {D.his}, found by a deputy who smelled marijuana from the group. {D} claimed the jacket before changing the story.", "Two identical jackets on a crowded bench, and a person who grabbed the wrong one. The State must prove {D} knew what was in the pocket."),
        timeline: [(0, "10:40 p.m.: the deputy arrives."), (0, "10:50 p.m.: the jacket is searched."), (0, "11 p.m.: {D} is cited."), (14, "The lab confirms marijuana.")],
        identified: "The jacket held {D}'s keys and wallet.",
        notDone: ["The other five people were never searched or questioned.", "The jacket's ownership was never confirmed by a seller or a friend."],
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let borrowedBikeV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.borrowedBike",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Neighbor Borrows Kayak for the Weekend and Lists It Online", "Hull Identification Number Matches Marketplace Listing"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole a kayak valued at $950 belonging to {V}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V} lent {D}, a neighbor, a kayak for a weekend trip on {DATE} and expected it back on Monday. Three days later {V} saw the same kayak listed for $400 on a marketplace page under {D}'s name. The hull identification number in the listing photo matched {V}'s kayak. {D} says {V} said the kayak could be sold.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Marketplace Listing", "A kayak listed for $400 under {D}'s account with the hull number visible."), E(.document, 3, "Purchase Receipt", "{V} bought the kayak for $950 with the hull number on the receipt."), E(.statement, 2, "{V}", "Lent the kayak for a weekend and expected it back."), E(.digital, 2, "Text Messages", "{V} asks for the kayak back on Monday and gets no reply.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Said I Could Sell", "{DL} says {V} said the kayak could be sold if it went unused."), E(.document, 1, "Old Text", "A months-old text where {V} jokes about selling it.")],
        role: "Kayak owner",
        exam: [.direct("How did {D} come to have your kayak?", "\"{D} lives down the street from me. I lent {DL} the kayak for a weekend trip on {DATE}, and I expected it back on Monday.\""), .direct("What kind of kayak is it?", "\"A sit-on-top touring model that I bought for $950. I have the receipt, and the hull identification number is printed on it.\""), .direct("What did you do when Monday came?", "\"I texted {DL} asking for the kayak back. I did not get a reply, and I texted again that evening.\""), .direct("What did you find later?", "\"Three days after the loan, I saw the same kayak listed for $400 on a marketplace page under {D.his} name.\""), .direct("How did you know it was yours?", "\"The listing photo showed the hull number on the stern, and it matched the number on my receipt. I also recognized a scratch near the cockpit.\""), .direct("Did you ever give the defendant permission to sell it?", "\"No. I lent it for a weekend. I never agreed to a sale at any price.\""), .cross("Did you once joke about selling the kayak?", "\"I made a joke months ago in a text that I might get rid of it. It was a joke, and I did not mean it.\""), .cross("Did you tell the defendant when the kayak was due back?", "\"I told {DL} Monday. I did not put it in writing the day I lent it, but my text on Monday said so.\""), .cross("Are you sure the listing was the defendant's account?", "\"The seller's name on the page was {DL}'s. I did not confirm who typed the listing.\""), .cross("Did you contact the defendant after you saw the listing?", "\"I did, and I did not get a satisfying answer. I contacted the Sheriff's Office afterward.\""), .cross("Did anyone else use the kayak while it was out?", "\"I don't know. {D.He} said it was just a weekend trip, and I didn't ask about other riders.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Paddling club member",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your connection to {D}?", "\"We paddle together in a club, and I have known {D} for several years. We are on the same chat group.\""), .direct("What do you know about the kayak?", "\"I saw the kayak at the launch that weekend. {DF} said it was borrowed from a neighbor who never used it.\""), .direct("Did the defendant say anything about selling it?", "\"Afterward, {DF} told the group that the neighbor had joked about selling it and said {D.he} might list it.\""), .direct("How did the club react?", "\"A few of us thought it was a bad idea without checking first. I told {DF} to ask the neighbor again.\""), .direct("Did the defendant seem to think it was fine?", "\"Yes. {DF} believed the joke counted. I told {DF} jokes are not contracts.\""), .direct("What did the defendant say when {V} complained?", "\"{DF} said {D.he} would pay it back and take the listing down. I don't know what came of it.\""), .cross("Did you see {V} give permission?", "\"No. I was not there when the kayak was lent. My knowledge of that comes secondhand from {DF}.\""), .cross("Did the defendant ask you whether it was okay?", "\"{DF} asked the group casually. Nobody said yes. A couple of us said to check with the owner.\""), .cross("Did you read the old text?", "\"I saw a screenshot. It was brief and sounded like a joke to me.\""), .cross("Was the listing taken down?", "\"I'm not sure when. I did not follow it.\""), .cross("Do you think {D} acted honestly?", "\"I think {D.he} was careless. I can't tell you what {D.he} was thinking.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} sold a borrowed kayak.", "{V} said the kayak could be sold."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry. It won't happen again.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} listed the kayak the day after the weekend trip.", "{V} had joked about selling it and {DL} took it seriously."),
        defendant: [.direct("How did you end up with the kayak?", "\"{V} lent it to me for a weekend trip. We have been neighbors for years, and {V} said the kayak was hardly ever used.\""), .direct("What did {V} say about selling it?", "\"Months earlier, {V} joked in a text that it was just taking up space and could be sold. I took that to mean I could sell it if it went unused.\""), .direct("Why did you list it for $400?", "\"It was a fair used price, and I figured I'd give {V} the money. I should have asked first.\""), .direct("Did you see {V}'s texts on Monday?", "\"I saw them. I didn't reply because I did not know what to say. I felt uneasy about it.\""), .direct("Did you tell the buyer it was borrowed?", "\"No. I did not tell anyone. That was a mistake.\""), .direct("What do you want to say to {V}?", "\"That I misunderstood the joke, and I am sorry. I'd pay {V} back.\""), .cross("You listed it the day after the trip, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I listed it the next day. I'm not hiding that.\""), .cross("The hull number in the photo is {V}'s, isn't it?", "\"Yes, it is. I took the photo of the kayak I borrowed.\""), .cross("{V} asked for it back on Monday, didn't {V.he}?", "\"Yes. I got the text. I did not return the kayak or answer it.\""), .cross("The joke about selling was months old, wasn't it?", "\"It was. I took it more seriously than it was meant, and I did not check.\""), .cross("You never asked {V} directly if you could sell it, did you?", "\"No. I did not ask. I assumed.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} lent {D} a $950 kayak for a weekend and asked for it back on Monday. Instead, the kayak appeared on a marketplace page for $400 under {D}'s name, with {V}'s hull number visible in the photo. You will see the receipt, the listing, and the unanswered texts.", "{D} borrowed a kayak from a neighbor who had joked in a text about selling it. {D} took the joke at face value, and there was no plan to cheat anyone. You will hear from a club member who heard {D} talk about it openly."),
        closings: ("The receipt and the listing carry the same hull number, and {D} listed the kayak the day after the loan. {V} asked for it back and got silence. A loan is not a gift, and {D} treated it as one.", "A months-old joke, an open listing under {D}'s own name, and a club chat where {D} talked about it freely do not describe someone hiding a theft. The club chat was never reviewed. The State must prove {D} knew the kayak was not {D.his} to sell."),
        timeline: [(0, "{V} lends the kayak."), (1, "{D} lists the kayak."), (2, "{V} asks for it back."), (3, "{V} sees the listing.")],
        identified: "The marketplace account is {D}'s.",
        notDone: ["The paddling club's chat was never reviewed.", "The listing's date was never checked against the loan."],
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let landfillSalvageV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.landfillSalvage",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Salvage Yard Entered at Night to Pull Catalytic Converters Despite Written Ban", "Gate Camera Shows Banned Customer Cutting the Fence"],
        law: "trespass2",
        spec: "Entered and remained on the premises of {V}, a salvage yard, after being notified not to, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A salvage yard banned {D} in writing six weeks before {DATE} after a customer complaint about stripped cars. At 11:15 p.m. on {DATE}, {D} cut a gap in the fence and went to a row of wrecked cars with a battery saw. The yard's camera recorded the entry. Deputies arrived at 11:55 p.m. {D} says the gap was already there.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Written Ban", "A signed ban six weeks earlier."), E(.video, 3, "Yard Camera", "{D} cuts the fence at 11:15 p.m. and enters."), E(.physical, 2, "Saw", "A battery saw and a bag of parts found at the fence."), E(.statement, 2, "Yard Owner", "The ban was handed to {D} at the counter.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Gap Already There", "{DL} says the gap was already there."), E(.document, 1, "Fence Photo", "A photo of a cut section of fence taken the week before.")],
        role: "Salvage yard owner",
        exam: [.direct("What did you do about {D} six weeks earlier?", "\"I handed {D} a written ban at the counter after a customer complaint about stripped cars. {D.He} signed it.\""), .direct("What does the yard camera show on the night in question?", "\"At 11:15 p.m., {D.he} cuts a gap in the fence and walks to a row of wrecked cars with a battery saw.\""), .direct("What was found at the fence?", "\"A battery saw and a bag of parts. Deputies arrived at 11:55.\""), .direct("Why did you ban the defendant?", "\"A customer complained that {DL} stripped parts off cars before paying for them. I handed {DL} a written ban at the counter and had it signed.\""), .direct("What did the camera show?", "\"At 11:15 p.m., {D.he} cut a gap in the fence with bolt cutters and went to a row of wrecked cars carrying a battery saw.\""), .direct("What did deputies find?", "\"A battery saw and a bag of parts at the fence line. {D.He} was still near the cars when the deputies arrived at 11:55.\""), .cross("{D} says the gap was already there, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"There had been a gap earlier. I cannot argue.\""), .cross("Does the defendant buy parts at the yard in the daytime?", "\"Often. {DL} was a regular customer until the ban.\""), .cross("Did anyone see the defendant cut the fence?", "\"The camera shows the cut. No person saw it.\""), .cross("A section of fence was cut before that night, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. A photo from the week before shows a cut section on the east side that I had not repaired yet.\""), .cross("You do not know who cut the first gap, do you?", "\"No. I only know about the cut on the camera that night, and I never saw the earlier one being made.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Salvage yard regular",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did the yard ban {D}?", "\"I heard so. I did not see the notice, but I heard it from others at the counter.\""), .direct("Is the gate open during the day?", "\"Yes. Customers walk in and out all day, and the yard is busy.\""), .direct("Did the defendant buy parts there often?", "\"Often. I saw {D} at the counter many times over the years.\""), .direct("How do you know the yard?", "\"I buy parts there often and know most of the regulars. I was in the yard the week before and saw the fence.\""), .direct("What did you see about the fence?", "\"A cut section on the east side that had been open for days. Customers walked around it and nobody fixed it.\""), .direct("Did you see the defendant that night?", "\"No. I only heard about it afterward from the owner and from other regulars at the counter.\""), .cross("Were you at the yard at night?", "\"No. I was never there at night. I only know the daytime yard.\""), .cross("Did you know about the fence gap?", "\"I saw a gap earlier that week. I did not report it.\""), .cross("Would a customer cut a fence at night to get parts?", "\"No. A customer would come in the daytime and pay.\""), .cross("You were not there when the defendant went in, were you?", "\"No. I was at home that evening, and I know about it only from what people said.\""), .cross("{D} had been banned, hadn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. Everyone at the yard knew about the ban, because the owner announced it at the counter.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} cut the fence and entered after a ban.", "{D} used an existing gap."),
        allocution: "\"I'm ashamed of it, Your Honor. I want to make it right.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} cut the fence a second time.", "The first gap was already there from earlier."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you cut the fence at the salvage yard?", "\"No. The gap was already there from earlier. I only went through it.\""), .direct("Did you know about the ban?", "\"Yes. I got the written ban. I ignored it because I needed the part.\""), .direct("What were you looking for?", "\"A set of alternators for a customer's car. I had been to the yard dozens of times and knew which rows had them.\""), .direct("Why did you go at night?", "\"The yard closes at five, and another customer told me the fence was already open on the east side. I did not want to wait for the weekend.\""), .direct("What about the ban?", "\"I knew about it, and I told myself the owner would not notice a quick visit. That was foolish, and I understand why it matters.\""), .direct("What did you do once you were inside the yard that night?", "\"I walked down the row looking for a battery and a few parts. I set the saw on a hood and was loading a bag when the lights came on.\""), .cross("The camera shows you cutting the fence, doesn't it?", "\"It shows me working at the fence. I widened a gap that was there.\""), .cross("You had a battery saw and a bag of parts, didn't you?", "\"Yes. The saw was for cutting the part. I should not have been there.\""), .cross("You were banned six weeks earlier and went back at night. Why?", "\"I was desperate. I should have found another way.\""), .cross("You cut the fence a second time, didn't you?", "\"Yes, to widen the gap enough to get through with my gear. I should not have touched it at all.\""), .cross("You had a battery saw with you, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I carry it for cutting bolts and brackets, and I planned to cut out the alternators.\"")],
        openings: ("A salvage yard banned {D} in writing six weeks earlier. At 11:15 p.m., the yard camera shows {D} cut a gap in the fence and enter a row of wrecked cars with a battery saw.", "The defense evidence will establish that the fence gap was already there from earlier and that {D} only widened it, with no plan to harm anyone."),
        closings: ("A signed ban, a fence cut at 11:15 p.m. on camera, a battery saw, and a bag of parts. {D} knew the yard was off limits.", "A gap that was already in the fence and a customer who went through it. The State must prove {D} cut the fence and knew entry was forbidden."),
        timeline: [(-42, "The yard gives {D} the written ban."), (0, "11:15 p.m.: {D} cuts the fence."), (0, "11:55 p.m.: deputies arrive."), (1, "The yard sends the camera video.")],
        identified: "The gate camera identifies {D}.",
        notDone: ["The saw's blade was never matched to the cut converters.", "The yard's inventory of the row was never checked."],
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let cellTowerClimbV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.cellTowerClimb",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Trespasser Climbs Water Tower Ladder for Night Photos Despite Posted Signs", "Water Authority Camera Shows Figure on Catwalk"],
        law: "trespass2",
        spec: "Entered and remained on the premises of {V}, a water authority, after being notified not to, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "At 10 p.m. on {DATE}, {D} climbed a fence into a water tower compound and went up the ladder to the catwalk for photographs. Signs on the fence warned of trespassing and a fall hazard. The authority's camera recorded {D} for forty minutes. Deputies arrived at 10:50 p.m. {D} says {D.he} did not see the signs in the dark.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Compound Camera", "{D} climbs the fence at 10:05 p.m. and the ladder at 10:12 p.m."), E(.document, 2, "Posted Signs", "Four warning signs on the fence reading 'No Trespassing'."), E(.physical, 2, "Camera Gear", "A tripod and camera found at the foot of the ladder."), E(.statement, 2, "Authority Technician", "Saw {D} on the tower camera and called deputies.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Dark", "{DL} says it was dark and {D.he} did not see the signs."), E(.document, 1, "Moon Data", "A near-new moon that night.")],
        role: "Water authority technician",
        exam: [.direct("What is your job with the water authority?", "\"I'm a technician. I monitor the tower cameras and maintain the compound. On {DATE} I was watching the screens at about ten at night.\""), .direct("What did you see on the camera?", "\"At 10:05 a person climbed the perimeter fence and walked toward the tower. At 10:12 that person started up the ladder.\""), .direct("How long was {D} on the tower?", "\"About forty minutes, according to the footage. {D} reached the catwalk, set up a camera, and took photographs of the skyline.\""), .direct("What signs are posted on the fence?", "\"Four of them, spaced along the fence line, reading No Trespassing and warning of a fall hazard. They are reflective on the lower half.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I called the Sheriff's Office. Deputies arrived at 10:50 and met {D.him} at the foot of the ladder, where a tripod and camera were set up.\""), .direct("Why is the tower off limits?", "\"It is a restricted utility site. A fall from the catwalk is lethal, and the ladder has a cage that is not meant for visitors.\""), .cross("Did you see the defendant read or pass the signs?", "\"The camera shows {DL} climbing at a place where a sign hangs, but I can't tell whether {DL} looked at it.\""), .cross("Was the compound lit at night?", "\"There is a floodlight at the gate, not on the side where {D.he} climbed. That side is mostly dark.\""), .cross("Did the defendant damage anything on the tower?", "\"No. I saw nothing broken or removed. {D.He} only climbed and took pictures.\""), .cross("Was the ladder cage locked?", "\"I believe it was supposed to be, but I have not inspected it. I don't know if the lock was engaged.\""), .cross("How dark was the night?", "\"Pretty dark. I understand there was almost no moon. The sign visibility at night was never tested.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Photographer friend",
        defenseExam: [.direct("How do you know {D}?", "\"We are photography friends. We go out together on weekends, and I met {D} through a local camera club.\""), .direct("Did the defendant talk about the tower?", "\"Yes. {D.He} said the tower had a great view and that {D.he} wanted a night shot of the city lights.\""), .direct("Were you there that night?", "\"No. I was in another town. Everything I have comes from {D.his} own words before and after.\""), .direct("How did the defendant sound afterward?", "\"Embarrassed and worried. {DF} told me that the signs were impossible to see in the dark, and that a deputy had been waiting.\""), .direct("Does the defendant take safety seriously?", "\"Yes. {D.He} always wears a harness at heights and checks gear. {D.He} is not reckless.\""), .direct("What was the moon like that night?", "\"A near-new moon, so very dark. I checked after hearing about it, and it was almost invisible.\""), .cross("Did you go to the tower with the defendant in daytime?", "\"I'm not going to say anything about that. I did not go with {D.him}.\""), .cross("Did {D} tell you about the fence?", "\"{D.He} said it was a chain-link fence and easy to climb. That's all.\""), .cross("Did the defendant mention signs before that night?", "\"Not to me. {D.He} did not say anything about signs until afterward.\""), .cross("Would you have gone up?", "\"No. I do not climb restricted structures. I'm not defending that part.\""), .cross("How good is the defendant's eyesight?", "\"Normal, I think. {D.He} wears no glasses I know of.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} climbed a posted tower for photos.", "{D} did not see the signs in the dark."),
        allocution: "\"I'm ashamed of it, Your Honor. I want to make it right.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had scouted the tower by day and read the signs.", "The signs were hard to see after dark."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you climb the tower?", "\"I'm a photographer, and I wanted a night shot of the skyline from that height. I'd seen the tower from the road and thought the view would be perfect.\""), .direct("Did you read the signs?", "\"I did not see any in the dark. I went over the fence on the far side from the gate, and I was focused on the ladder.\""), .direct("What did you carry?", "\"A tripod and a camera. I did not bring anything else, and I did not touch the tower equipment.\""), .direct("Were you afraid of falling?", "\"A little, yes. I stayed on the catwalk and held the rail. I was careful.\""), .direct("What happened when deputies arrived?", "\"I saw their lights and climbed down right away. I answered all their questions and told them I did not see any signs.\""), .direct("Would you have gone up if you'd seen the signs?", "\"No. I would not have gone onto a restricted site. I was careless in the dark.\""), .cross("You climbed a fence to get in, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I climbed over. I did not see a gate that was open.\""), .cross("A fence with signs on it is meant to keep people out, isn't it?", "\"It is, and I know that. I'm saying I did not see the signs.\""), .cross("You were there forty minutes, weren't you?", "\"About that, yes. I was setting up long exposures.\""), .cross("You visited the tower during the day beforehand, didn't you?", "\"I'd rather say only what I'm sure about. I looked at it from the road earlier.\""), .cross("Did you tell anyone you were going up?", "\"No. I went alone, and I did not ask anyone.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} climbed a fence into a restricted water tower compound at 10:05 p.m., went up the ladder to the catwalk, and stayed forty minutes taking photographs. Four warning signs hang on the fence. The authority's camera and a tripod at the foot of the ladder tell the story.", "It was almost a moonless night, and {D} climbed in at the dark side of the compound, far from the gate light. {D} says the signs were invisible, and no one ever tested whether they could be seen at night. {D} did no damage and came down at once."),
        closings: ("A fence, four signs, a ladder, and forty minutes at a height that can kill. {D} climbed past all of it with a tripod. The camera shows every step.", "On a moonless night with the signs on the dark side of the fence, {D} did not see what the State says was plain. The signs' visibility at night was never tested. The State must prove {D} knew the site was off limits."),
