        defendant: [.direct("Were you riding between lanes at 80 miles per hour?", "\"I was riding on the shoulder and between cars, but I believed I was going with traffic, and I did not think it was 80.\""), .direct("Why did you ride on the shoulder?", "\"Traffic ahead was stopped for a crash. I wanted to get past it, and I thought the shoulder was clear enough.\""), .direct("What about the helmet camera video?", "\"It shows what it shows. I posted the ride because I was proud of it. I did not think about how it would look.\""), .direct("What was your ride that day?", "\"A commute home on a motorcycle I have owned for six years. I was filming my rides with a helmet camera and had posted some online.\""), .direct("Why were you on the shoulder?", "\"Cars ahead were creeping and I thought the shoulder was clear. I stayed to the right and tried to keep my speed with the flow.\""), .direct("What did you think about your speed?", "\"I thought I was keeping pace with moving traffic. Looking at the video later, I can see the cars were stopped.\""), .cross("The radar read 80 miles per hour, didn't it?", "\"Yes. That is what the radar says. I did not look at the speedometer. I do not dispute the number.\""), .cross("You passed cars within inches, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I know it was close. I felt in control at the time, but I see now it was reckless.\""), .cross("You kept going when a trooper chased you, didn't you?", "\"I did not realize at first. When I did, I pulled over.\""), .cross("The speedometer in your own video reads 80, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. I did not notice at the time, and I cannot argue with my own footage.\""), .cross("You posted that ride on social media, didn't you?", "\"Yes, the clip went up that evening. I did not think about how it would look to a trooper.\"")],
        openings: ("With traffic stopped for a crash on a four-lane highway, {D} rode a motorcycle onto the shoulder and between lanes at about 80 miles per hour, passing within inches of cars. A trooper chased {D} for two miles.", "The defense witnesses will explain that traffic had been moving slowly, that {D} believed {D.he} was riding at the speed of traffic, and that no one was hurt."),
        closings: ("Eighty miles per hour on a narrow shoulder past stopped cars, inches from drivers, with the speedometer on the helmet camera. {D} even posted the ride online.", "A rider who thought traffic was moving and did not see the danger. The State must prove {D} knowingly rode recklessly, and the evidence of speed does not prove that."),
