        exam: [.direct("What happened when {D} came through your screening station?", "\"At 9:10 a.m., I asked if {D} had any weapons, and {D.he} said no. During a pat down, I found a switchblade in the cuff of {D.his} boot.\""), .direct("What kind of knife was it?", "\"A switchblade with a three-inch blade. The screening camera shows me finding it at 9:12.\""), .direct("What is posted at the entrance?", "\"A list at the courthouse door that bars knives and other weapons. It is large and easy to see.\""), .direct("What is your job at the courthouse?", "\"I screen everyone entering the building, checking bags and using a wand and a pat down when something sets off the alarm. I do it for about two hundred people a day.\""), .direct("What happened at the station?", "\"I asked {D.him} if there were any weapons, and {D.he} said no. The wand beeped at the boot, and I found a switchblade with a three-inch blade tucked in the cuff.\""), .direct("How is the weapons rule posted?", "\"A list of banned items is on the door and again at the station, with knives at the top. It is large print and easy to see.\""), .cross("{D} says {D.he} forgot the knife was in the boot, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. {DL} said that right away. I will agree {DL} did not try to hide it from me.\""), .cross("Was {D} there for a traffic matter?", "\"Yes. It was a traffic matter. {D.He} was not there for anything serious.\""), .cross("Did the defendant resist the pat down?", "\"No. {D.He} was cooperative and polite.\""), .cross("{D} was cooperative once the knife was found, wasn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. {D.He} handed it over and said it was from a camping trip.\""), .cross("The knife was hidden in a boot cuff, not in a pocket, was it?", "\"Yes, in the cuff. That is a place people sometimes forget, and I have seen it before.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Coworker",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Does {D} carry a knife at work?", "\"A pocketknife, for opening boxes. I have seen it many times at the shop where we both work.\""), .direct("Is that knife a switchblade?", "\"I do not think so. It was a regular folding knife the way I saw it, not the spring-loaded kind.\""), .direct("Did the defendant wear the same boots every day?", "\"Daily. {D} wore those boots to work every day, and I saw them all the time.\""), .direct("How do you know the defendant?", "\"We work together on the same crew. I know {D.him} to be careful and calm.\""), .direct("What did the defendant say about the knife?", "\"That it was from a weekend camping trip and had slipped from {D.his} mind. {D.He} showed me photos from the campsite.\""), .direct("What do you know about the defendant's habits?", "\"{D.He} keeps a pocketknife in the work truck and sometimes in a boot. It is for cutting rope and boxes.\""), .cross("Did {D} tell you about going to the courthouse?", "\"No. {D.He} did not mention it to me, so I did not think to ask about the knife.\""), .cross("Did you ever see the defendant put a knife in the boot?", "\"No. I never saw that. I only know about the pocketknife.\""), .cross("Did the defendant go camping recently?", "\"I heard about a trip. I do not know details.\""), .cross("You were not at the courthouse that morning, were you?", "\"No. I only know what {D.he} told me afterward.\""), .cross("A switchblade is not a camping knife, is it?", "\"Some people carry them for camping. I would not, but I know people who do.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} carried a concealed switchblade into a courthouse.", "{D} forgot the knife in a boot."),
        allocution: "\"I let things get out of hand.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had carried the knife in the boot all week.", "The knife was left from a camping trip and {DL} forgot it."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you know the knife was in your boot?", "\"No. I forgot it was there. It had been in the boot since a camping trip, and I did not think about it.\""), .direct("Why did you tell the screener you had no weapons?", "\"Because I believed that. I had forgotten about the knife, and I answered honestly.\""), .direct("Did you read the posted list at the door?", "\"I saw it, but I did not think about my boots. I was nervous about the traffic matter.\""), .direct("Why were you at the courthouse?", "\"I was there for a traffic ticket hearing. I wore my work boots because I came straight from a job.\""), .direct("How did the knife get in your boot?", "\"I carried it on a camping trip three days before and tucked it in the boot for safekeeping. I never took it out.\""), .direct("What did you say when asked about weapons?", "\"I said no, because at that moment I honestly did not think of the knife. I felt sick when it was found.\""), .cross("A switchblade is not a pocketknife, is it?", "\"It is a different kind of knife. I should have known better than to leave it there.\""), .cross("You told a screener you had no weapons and the knife was in your boot. How is that honest?", "\"I believed I had none. I had forgotten it, and I apologize.\""), .cross("The notice was posted at the door, wasn't it?", "\"Yes, and I walked past it. I did not look at the list closely.\""), .cross("You had carried that knife in your boot all week, hadn't you?", "\"Yes, and I went to work with it. I did not think about it until the wand beeped.\""), .cross("You were told twice that the courthouse bars knives, weren't you?", "\"Yes, there was a sign and the screener said it. I said no because I had forgotten about the knife. I know that is hard to believe.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} walked through the screening station at a county courthouse for a traffic matter. A screener asked about weapons, {D} said no, and a pat down found a switchblade in the cuff of {D}'s boot, with a posted list barring knives at the door.", "The defense case is that the knife was left from a camping trip, that {D} forgot it was in the boot, and that {D} cooperated with the screener."),
        closings: ("A posted list barring knives, a question about weapons, a denial, and a switchblade in the boot. {D} carried it into a courthouse.", "A forgotten knife from a camping trip in a boot {D} wore every day. The State must prove {D} knew it was there, and forgetting is not a crime."),
        timeline: [(0, "9:10 a.m.: {D} reaches the screening station."), (0, "9:12 a.m.: the knife is found."), (0, "9:20 a.m.: deputies take the report."), (1, "The courthouse sends the screening video.")],
        identified: "The screener found the knife on {D}.",
        notDone: ["The knife's mechanism was never tested.", "The boot's work history was never confirmed."],
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let voicemailThreatBossV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.voicemailThreatBoss",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Tenant Sticks Note on Landlord's Door Threatening to Burn Building", "Handwriting and Camera Tie Note to Evicted Tenant"],
        law: "communicatingThreats",
        spec: "Willfully threatened to damage the property of {V}, a landlord, by fire, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After an eviction notice, a note was found on {V}'s office door on {DATE} that read 'I'll burn this building down.' The note was written in block letters on the back of a rent notice. A hallway camera shows {D} at the door at 9:10 p.m. A handwriting examiner found similarities with {D}'s lease signature. {D} says it was anger and was never meant to be taken seriously.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Note", "A note in block letters on the back of a rent notice reading 'I'll burn this building down.'"), E(.video, 3, "Hallway Camera", "{D} stands at the office door at 9:10 p.m. and leaves a paper."), E(.document, 2, "Examiner Report", "Similarities between the note's lettering and {D}'s lease signature."), E(.statement, 2, "{V}", "Found the note at 7 a.m. and called deputies.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Anger", "{DL} says it was anger and never meant seriously."), E(.document, 1, "Eviction Notice", "An eviction notice received three days before.")],
        role: "Landlord",
        exam: [.direct("What did the handwriting examiner find?", "\"Similarities between the note's lettering and {D}'s lease signature. I called deputies right away.\""), .direct("What did you find on the door?", "\"At seven in the morning, a rent notice taped to my office door with block letters on the back reading, I will burn this building down. I called deputies immediately.\""), .direct("What did the hallway camera show?", "\"{D.He} stands at my door at 9:10 the night before and leaves a folded paper. {D.He} walks away without looking at the camera.\""), .direct("Why did you evict {D}?", "\"{D.He} was months behind on rent. I served a notice three days earlier, and {D.he} was angry when it was delivered.\""), .direct("What did you do when you found the note on your office door?", "\"I read it twice, took a photo of it where it hung, and called the sheriff's office. I also made sure no one was in the building.\""), .direct("What had you and the defendant discussed before the eviction?", "\"{D.He} fell behind on rent for several months. We had two meetings about a payment plan, and {D.he} was angry both times.\""), .cross("{D} says it was anger and not a serious threat, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. {D.He} was very angry about the eviction. I understand that, but it frightened me.\""), .cross("Did the defendant mention fire to you before?", "\"No. {D.He} never mentioned fire.\""), .cross("Was the examiner certain?", "\"No. The report says similarities, not certainty.\""), .cross("The note was not signed, was it?", "\"No signature. I know it only from the camera and the examiner's report on the lettering.\""), .cross("{D} has never been violent, has {D.he}?", "\"Not that I have seen. {D.He} shouted at me once over the phone, but never touched anything.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Fellow tenant",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did {D} ever write threats to anyone?", "\"Never. In all the time I have known {D}, I never saw anything threatening. {D.He} complained but did not threaten.\""), .direct("Was the defendant angry about the eviction?", "\"Very. {D.He} was upset and hurt about losing the apartment, and we talked about it in the hallway.\""), .direct("Did the defendant ever mention fire?", "\"No. Not once. I never heard {D.him} say anything about fire or burning.\""), .direct("How do you know the defendant?", "\"We live on the same floor, and I have talked with {DF} many times. I know {DF} as a quiet neighbor.\""), .direct("How did the defendant react to the notice?", "\"{D.He} was upset and said some harsh things in the hallway. It was anger, not a plan.\""), .direct("Did {D} ever mention burning anything?", "\"Never to me. I would have taken it seriously.\""), .cross("Did you see the note itself?", "\"After it was found. I saw the paper and the block letters, and I did not recognize the writing.\""), .cross("Did the defendant leave town after the eviction notice?", "\"I heard {DF} left for a week. I do not know why.\""), .cross("Could the defendant have written a note when angry?", "\"Anyone can write something when angry. I cannot say that {D.he} did.\""), .cross("You did not see the note being written, did you?", "\"No. I only heard about it afterward.\""), .cross("{D} left town after the note, didn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes, for a week. I thought it was to cool down.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} threatened to burn a building.", "{D} wrote it in anger and meant nothing."),
        allocution: "\"I let things get out of hand.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had bought lighter fluid the next day.", "{DL} was angry and left town for a week."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you write the note?", "\"I left a paper at the door when I was furious. I was angry about the eviction, and I did not mean it seriously.\""), .direct("Did you intend to burn the building?", "\"No. I never intended to burn anything. It was anger, and I never would have acted on it.\""), .direct("Why did you leave town afterward?", "\"I needed time to cool off and think. I went to stay with a relative for a week.\""), .direct("How did you feel about the eviction?", "\"Furious and scared. I had lost my job and had nowhere to go, and I felt like I was being thrown out on the street.\""), .direct("What did you write?", "\"In a burst of anger, I wrote that I would burn the building down. I left it on the office door and went home.\""), .direct("What happened afterward?", "\"I left town for a week to cool off. I did not intend to act on it, and I never went near a lighter that night.\""), .cross("The examiner found similarities to your lease signature, didn't the examiner?", "\"Similarities. Not a match. I do not think it is my writing.\""), .cross("You were at the door at 9:10 p.m. Why?", "\"To leave a note. I should not have written what I did.\""), .cross("You bought lighter fluid the next day, didn't you?", "\"Yes, for a grill at a relative's place. It looks bad, and I understand why it worries people.\""), .cross("You wrote the words on the back of a rent notice, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It was a piece of paper at hand, and I used it without thinking.\""), .cross("You left town right after the note was left, didn't you?", "\"I left the next morning. I was angry and needed to cool off, and I stayed with a relative. I did not intend to burn anything.\"")],
        openings: ("After an eviction notice, a note was found on {V}'s office door reading 'I'll burn this building down,' written in block letters on the back of a rent notice. A hallway camera shows {D} at the door at 9:10 p.m., and an examiner found similarities to {D}'s lease signature.", "Weigh the defense proof, which will show that {D} was angry about the eviction, never meant the words seriously, and left a paper on the door in frustration."),
        closings: ("A note threatening fire, {D} at the door on camera, lettering that resembles {D}'s signature, and lighter fluid bought the next day. {V} had every reason to be afraid.", "An angry tenant and an examiner who found only similarities. The State must prove {D} wrote a real threat, and words of anger without intent are not a threat."),
        timeline: [(-3, "{D} receives the eviction notice."), (0, "9:10 p.m.: {D} leaves the note."), (0, "7 a.m.: {V} finds the note."), (1, "{V} reports it to the Sheriff's Office.")],
        identified: "The hallway camera and the handwriting tie the note to {D}.",
        notDone: ["The note's handwriting was never compared by an expert.", "The hallway camera's time stamp was never checked."],
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let stolenTrailerHitchV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.stolenTrailerHitch",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Riding Mower With Ground-Off Serial Number Found in Barn After Theft Report", "Auction Receipt Does Not Match Mower Serial"],
        law: "possStolen",
        spec: "Possessed a riding mower valued at $2,400 belonging to {V}, knowing or having reason to know it was stolen, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V} reported a riding mower stolen from a shed on {DATE}. A deputy found the same model mower in {D}'s barn with the serial plate ground off and the hood repainted. The mower's engine number matched {V}'s purchase records. {D} says {D.he} bought the mower at an auction and the seller gave a receipt.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Mower", "A riding mower with the serial plate ground off and a repainted hood."), E(.document, 3, "Engine Number", "The engine number matches {V}'s purchase records."), E(.document, 2, "Auction Receipt", "A receipt for a mower with no serial number listed."), E(.video, 2, "Barn Search Video", "A deputy finds the mower under a tarp.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Bought at Auction", "{DL} says {D.he} bought the mower at an auction."), E(.document, 1, "Auction Listing", "A listing of 'assorted lawn equipment' for the week.")],
        role: "Mower owner",
        exam: [.direct("What was stolen from your shed?", "\"A riding mower. I reported it stolen, and a deputy later found the same model in {D}'s barn.\""), .direct("What was different about the mower the deputy found?", "\"The serial plate had been ground off and the hood repainted. The engine number matches my purchase records.\""), .direct("How was it found?", "\"Under a tarp in {D.his} barn. The deputy's search video shows it.\""), .direct("What was stolen?", "\"A riding mower with a forty-two inch deck, stored in my shed. I noticed the shed door was open and the mower gone on the morning of the report.\""), .direct("How did you identify it?", "\"A deputy called me to a barn where a mower sat under a tarp. The engine number matched my purchase records exactly.\""), .direct("What had been done to the mower?", "\"The serial plate was ground off and the hood was repainted a different green. It looked like it had been disguised.\""), .cross("{D} says {D.he} bought the mower at an auction, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. {D.He} produced a receipt for a mower with no serial number listed.\""), .cross("Could another mower have the same engine number?", "\"No. Engine numbers are unique, and it matches mine.\""), .cross("Did anyone see the defendant take the mower?", "\"No. No one saw it taken from my shed.\""), .cross("You never saw the mower in the defendant's barn before the deputy did, did you?", "\"No. I only learned of it when the deputy called.\""), .cross("Many mowers of that model exist, don't they?", "\"Yes. But the engine number is unique, and it was mine.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Auction regular",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did {D} buy mowers at your auction?", "\"Often. {D} is a regular and buys small engines and mowers there every few weeks.\""), .direct("Did you see this particular mower sold?", "\"I cannot say. We sell dozens of mowers, and I do not remember each one.\""), .direct("Does the auction check serial numbers?", "\"Not always. We check some items, but many small engines go out without a serial check.\""), .direct("How do you know about the auction?", "\"I go regularly and buy tools and mowers. I was there the day {DF} bought one.\""), .direct("What did you see?", "\"A lot of lawn equipment sold in lots. {D.He} bought a mower and paid with cash.\""), .direct("What are the receipts like?", "\"Handwritten, with an item and a price. They rarely list serial numbers.\""), .cross("Does your auction give receipts for every sale?", "\"Sometimes. For cash sales, we often write a short slip with no serial number.\""), .cross("Would you sell a mower with the serial plate ground off?", "\"No. I would not knowingly. It would be a red flag.\""), .cross("Do you know who sold the mower to the auction?", "\"No. I do not know. We take consignments from many sellers.\""), .cross("You do not know where the auction got the mower, do you?", "\"No. I only know that equipment is brought in by many sellers.\""), .cross("You did not see the defendant sand or paint anything, did you?", "\"No. I only saw {DF} buy and load a mower.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} had a stolen mower with the serial removed.", "{D} bought the mower at an auction."),
        allocution: "\"It was a stupid decision and someone else paid for it.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} ground the serial plate off and repainted the hood.", "The auction was real and {DL} did buy a mower there."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you steal {V}'s mower?", "\"No. I bought the mower at an auction, and the seller gave me a receipt.\""), .direct("Did you grind the serial plate off?", "\"No. It was already like that when I bought it. I did not touch the plate.\""), .direct("Why did you repaint the hood?", "\"The paint was faded. I painted it to make it look better, and I did not know it was stolen.\""), .direct("How did you come by the mower?", "\"I bought it at an auction of assorted lawn equipment and was handed a receipt. It had no serial number listed.\""), .direct("Why was the hood repainted?", "\"I repainted it because it was faded. I wanted to resell the mower, and I did not notice the serial plate was missing.\""), .direct("What did you do when the deputy came?", "\"I showed the receipt and told the deputy where I bought it. I did not hide the mower.\""), .cross("The engine number matches {V}'s purchase records, doesn't it?", "\"I know. I did not check it. I trusted the auction.\""), .cross("Your receipt lists no serial number, does it?", "\"No. It was a simple slip. I did not think to ask for more.\""), .cross("A mower with no serial plate did not make you suspicious?", "\"It should have. I am sorry.\""), .cross("You ground off the serial plate, didn't you?", "\"Yes, because it was rusty and damaged. I thought a rusty plate was no loss.\""), .cross("You grew up around machines like that one, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I know how to take a plate off. I did that after I bought the mower, because the serial had rusted and could not be read.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} reported a riding mower stolen from a shed, and a deputy found the same model in {D}'s barn with the serial plate ground off and the hood repainted. The engine number matches {V}'s purchase records.", "Jurors will hear that {D} bought the mower at a real auction, received a receipt, and did not know it was stolen."),
        closings: ("A stolen mower, an engine number that matches, a serial plate ground off, and a new coat of paint in {D}'s barn. {D} hid what the mower was.", "An auction sale with a simple receipt and no serial number. The State must prove {D} knew the mower was stolen and altered it."),
        timeline: [(0, "{V} reports the mower stolen."), (2, "A deputy finds the mower in {D}'s barn."), (2, "The engine number is read."), (5, "{V} supplies the purchase records.")],
        identified: "The mower was found in {D}'s barn.",
        notDone: ["The auction house was never asked for a sales record.", "The engine number match was never confirmed by a second expert."],
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let fakeParkingTicketV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.fakeParkingTicket",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Man Posts Fake Park-and-Ride Fee Notices on Windshields With QR Code", "Transit Lot Notices Lead Drivers to Payment Page Under {D}'s Name"],
        law: "forgery",
        spec: "Falsely made parking fee notices with intent to defraud, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "On {DATE}, notices claiming an unpaid park-and-ride fee were found on 40 windshields in a transit lot, each with a QR code leading to a payment page. Two drivers paid $35 each before the transit agency posted a warning. The payment page and the QR account were registered to {D}. {D} says the notices were a prank for a class.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Notices", "Forty printed notices with a QR code and a fake agency logo."), E(.digital, 3, "Payment Page", "A payment page registered to an account in {D}'s name."), E(.document, 2, "Payment Records", "Two $35 payments received from drivers."), E(.statement, 2, "Transit Officer", "Collected forty notices and posted a warning.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Class Prank", "{DL} says the notices were a class prank and that {D.he} never meant to collect money."), E(.document, 1, "Course Syllabus", "A marketing class syllabus that lists a 'guerrilla ad' assignment.")],
        role: "Transit officer",
        exam: [.direct("What is your role with the transit agency?", "\"I'm a transit officer. I patrol the park-and-ride lots and respond to complaints. On the morning of {DATE} I was called to a lot about unusual notices.\""), .direct("What did you find on the windshields?", "\"Forty printed notices tucked under wipers, claiming an unpaid park-and-ride fee, with a QR code and what looked like an agency logo.\""), .direct("Was the logo genuine?", "\"No. It was a fake version of our logo, slightly off in the colors and the font. We do not issue fees on windshields.\""), .direct("What happened if a driver scanned the code?", "\"It led to a payment page that asked for a card number and charged $35. Two drivers paid before we posted a warning.\""), .direct("How did you trace the page?", "\"The payment page and the QR code account were registered to {D}, through the processor's records. That was about four days after the notices appeared.\""), .direct("What did you do with the notices?", "\"I collected all forty at noon, bagged them as evidence, and posted a warning at the lot entrance for the drivers.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} put the notices out?", "\"No. I did not see anyone place them. I identified {D.him} through the payment account.\""), .cross("Did anyone report what the person who placed them looked like?", "\"No one. A few drivers saw the notices when they came back to their cars. They did not see who left them.\""), .cross("Did you ask the instructor about a class assignment?", "\"No. I did not contact the school or any instructor. I own that.\""), .cross("Did you speak to the two drivers who paid?", "\"I took the amounts from the processor's records. I did not interview them on what they saw.\""), .cross("Did the defendant keep the payments?", "\"I only know that the money landed in the account. What was done with it afterward I can't tell you.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Classmate",
        defenseExam: [.direct("How do you know {D}?", "\"We are in the same marketing class. We worked on separate projects but sat near each other all semester.\""), .direct("What was the assignment?", "\"A guerrilla ad. The syllabus lists it, and the instructor wanted us to design something unconventional that grabbed attention.\""), .direct("Did the defendant talk about the project?", "\"Yes, {D} mentioned wanting to do something with a parking notice. I thought it was a clever idea at the time.\""), .direct("Did the defendant mention payments?", "\"No, not to me. I did not know there was a payment page until I heard about the investigation.\""), .direct("What did your own project look like?", "\"Chalk art on a sidewalk. We were all told to be creative, and no one was supposed to charge money.\""), .direct("How did the defendant act afterward?", "\"Nervous. {DF} told me something had gone wrong and that people had paid. {DF} seemed sick about it.\""), .cross("Did the instructor approve the parking notices?", "\"I don't know. I never heard the instructor say anything about them.\""), .cross("Did you see the notices?", "\"I saw a photo afterward. They looked official, more than I'd expect for a class project.\""), .cross("Was a payment page part of the assignment?", "\"Not as far as I know. The assignment was about attention, not money.\""), .cross("Did the defendant ask you for advice?", "\"No. I did not know until it became a problem.\""), .cross("Did {D} plan to keep the money?", "\"I don't know. All I can pass along is that {DF} had not meant for anyone to pay.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} posted fake fee notices to collect money.", "{D} made them for a class."),
        allocution: "\"I knew better. I want to make it right.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} cashed out the two payments the same day.", "{DL} did have a class assignment but never told the instructor."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you make the notices?", "\"It was for a marketing class that had a guerrilla ad assignment. We were supposed to design something that grabbed attention.\""), .direct("Why did you put them on windshields?", "\"I thought it would be a realistic test of whether people notice flyers. I wasn't thinking about the fact that they looked official.\""), .direct("Why was there a payment page?", "\"I built it to make the stunt feel real. I didn't think anyone would actually pay. I was shocked when two people did.\""), .direct("What did you do when you saw the payments?", "\"I did not know what to do. I panicked and did nothing for a day or two. That was a mistake.\""), .direct("Did you tell your instructor?", "\"No, I did not. I was embarrassed and afraid I'd be in trouble.\""), .direct("What would you do differently?", "\"Everything. I should have used a fake name, or never involved a payment page. I should have returned the money.\""), .cross("You copied the agency logo, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I copied it from their website. I did not think about it being illegal.\""), .cross("Two people paid $35 because of your notices, didn't they?", "\"Yes. I feel terrible about those two. I should have refunded them immediately.\""), .cross("The payment page was in your name, wasn't it?", "\"Yes, my name and my account. I wasn't trying to hide it, which should tell you something.\""), .cross("You never told the instructor about the plan, did you?", "\"I did not. I was going to turn in the results at the end.\""), .cross("You kept the money for several days, didn't you?", "\"The money was in the account, and I did not touch it right away. I did not return it either.\"")],
        openings: ("Forty windshields in a transit lot carried a notice for an unpaid fee with a QR code and a fake agency logo. Two drivers paid $35 each, and the payment page was registered to {D}. You will hear from the transit officer who collected the notices and traced the account.", "{D} was working on a guerrilla ad assignment for a marketing class and built something that looked far too real. A course syllabus lists the assignment. {D} never meant for anyone to pay, and was horrified when two people did."),
        closings: ("A fake logo, a payment page with a card form, forty windshields, and two drivers out $35 each. The account is {D}'s. A class project does not ask for card numbers.", "The syllabus lists a guerrilla ad assignment, and {D} put the payment page in {D.his} own name. The instructor was never asked and the paying drivers were never interviewed. The State must prove {D} meant to take money, not make a point."),
        timeline: [(0, "Morning: the notices are placed."), (0, "Noon: officers collect them."), (2, "Two payments arrive."), (4, "The agency traces the page to {D}.")],
        identified: "The payment page is registered to {D}.",
        notDone: ["The instructor was never asked about the assignment.", "The two paying drivers were never asked what they saw."],
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let schoolPermitForgeV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.schoolPermitForge",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Student Athlete Forges Doctor's Signature on Sports Physical Form", "Clinic Stamp and Signature Do Not Match Records"],
        law: "forgery",
        spec: "Falsely made a physician's signature on a sports physical form with intent to defraud, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "{D}, a community college student, submitted a sports physical form to a coach on {DATE} signed by a doctor and stamped with a clinic seal. The college health office called the clinic, and the doctor said {D} was never examined and that the signature was not the doctor's own. The stamp was an older version no longer in use. {D} says a clinic employee signed it.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Physical Form", "A form with a physician signature and an old clinic stamp."), E(.statement, 3, "Clinic Doctor", "Never examined {D} and did not sign the form."), E(.document, 2, "Clinic Records", "No appointment for {D} in the prior year."), E(.document, 2, "Coach's Receipt", "The form was handed in on {DATE} with a roster signup.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Clinic Employee", "{DL} says a clinic employee signed the form."), E(.document, 1, "Appointment Text", "A text confirming a visit at the clinic for a different date.")],
        role: "College health office worker",
        exam: [.direct("What did {D} submit to the coach?", "\"A sports physical form signed by a doctor and stamped with a clinic seal. It was handed in with a roster signup.\""), .direct("What did you learn when you called the clinic?", "\"The doctor said {D} was never examined and that the signature on the form was not the doctor's own.\""), .direct("What about the stamp and the clinic records?", "\"The stamp was an older version no longer in use, and the clinic has no appointment for {D.him} in the prior year.\""), .direct("What do you do at the health office?", "\"I process physical forms for student athletes and verify them with the clinics. I call clinics when something looks off.\""), .direct("What looked off about this form?", "\"The stamp was an old version the clinic stopped using last year, and the signature looked rushed. I called the clinic to check.\""), .direct("What did the clinic say?", "\"The doctor said {D.he} was never examined and did not sign the form. The clinic had no appointment for {D.him} in the prior year.\""), .cross("{D} says a clinic employee signed the form, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. {D.He} said that. The clinic says no employee would sign for the doctor.\""), .cross("Did {D} visit the clinic at all?", "\"I heard {DL} did once. The clinic has no appointment record.\""), .cross("Did the clinic confirm right away that the form was false?", "\"Not at first. We called again the next day to be sure.\""), .cross("{D} did visit the clinic once, didn't {D.he}?", "\"A text shows a visit for a different date. It was not for a physical.\""), .cross("You do not know who signed it, do you?", "\"No. I only know the doctor did not.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Team trainer",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did {D} bring you the physical form first?", "\"To me first, before the coach. {D} handed it in at the training room.\""), .direct("Did the form look signed?", "\"It looked it. It had a signature and a clinic stamp, so I did not question it at the time.\""), .direct("Did the clinic confirm the form right away?", "\"Not at first. We called and were told to try again, and it took a day to get a clear answer.\""), .direct("What do you do for the team?", "\"I am the team trainer and collect physical forms from players. I keep them in a folder.\""), .direct("How did the defendant hand in the form?", "\"With a roster signup, on the due date. I put it in the folder without checking it.\""), .direct("What did you notice about the defendant?", "\"A hard-working player who showed up early. I had no reason to doubt the form.\""), .cross("Did you call the doctor yourself to check?", "\"The next day. I called, and the doctor said {D.he} was never examined.\""), .cross("Would a signed form usually be checked before the season?", "\"Usually, yes. We should have called sooner. That was our mistake.\""), .cross("Did the defendant seem nervous about the form?", "\"No. {D.He} seemed normal. I did not notice anything odd.\""), .cross("You do not verify signatures, do you?", "\"No. That is for the health office.\""), .cross("You did not see who signed it, did you?", "\"No. I only handled it after it was handed in.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} forged a doctor's signature on a sports form.", "A clinic employee signed the form."),
        allocution: "\"I took advantage of someone who trusted me, and I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had copied the signature from a friend's old form.", "{DL} did visit the clinic once and was told it would be signed later."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you forge the doctor's signature?", "\"No. I did not sign anything. A clinic employee gave me the form, and I thought it was signed properly.\""), .direct("Did you visit the clinic?", "\"Once. I was told the form would be signed later. I picked it up, and it had a signature.\""), .direct("Why was the stamp old?", "\"I do not know. I did not notice. I assumed the clinic knew what it was doing.\""), .direct("How did you get the form?", "\"I visited the clinic and was told the physical would be signed later. A friend gave me an old form and I used it to hurry.\""), .direct("Who signed it?", "\"I thought a clinic employee did when I picked it up. The signature copied from my friend's old form was used for the rest.\""), .direct("Why did you turn it in?", "\"I needed to join the team and did not want to miss the roster date. I thought it was close enough.\""), .cross("You never had an exam, did you?", "\"No. I did not. I thought a signature was all I needed.\""), .cross("You copied a friend's old form, didn't you?", "\"No. I did not. That is not true.\""), .cross("The doctor says the signature is not the doctor's. Who made it?", "\"I do not know. Someone at the clinic, I thought.\""), .cross("The doctor never examined you, did the doctor?", "\"No. I only had a quick visit about something else.\""), .cross("You copied a signature, didn't you?", "\"Yes, from a friend's old form. I know that is forgery.\"")],
        openings: ("{D}, a community college student, handed a coach a sports physical signed by a doctor and stamped with a clinic seal. The doctor says {D} was never examined and the signature is not the doctor's, and the stamp is an old version.", "By the end of this trial, the proof will show that {D} visited the clinic, was told the form would be signed later, and believed a clinic employee had signed it properly."),
        closings: ("A form with a forged signature, an old stamp, no appointment on record, and a doctor who never examined {D}. {D} handed it in.", "A student who went to the clinic and received a signed form. The State must prove {D} knew the signature was forged."),
        timeline: [(-7, "{D} visits the clinic for a different appointment."), (0, "{D} submits the form to the coach."), (1, "The health office calls the clinic."), (2, "The doctor denies signing the form.")],
        identified: "The submitted form came from {D}.",
        notDone: ["The clinic's stamp was never compared with the seal on the form.", "The friend who offered help was never identified."],
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let carBreakinGymV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.carBreakinGym",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Hospital Garage Window Smashed and Laptop Bag Taken From Back Seat", "Parking Garage Camera Shows Figure With Hammer"],
        law: "breakingVehicle",
        spec: "Broke or entered a motor vehicle of {V} with intent to commit larceny therein, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V} parked in a hospital garage at 7:30 a.m. on {DATE} with a laptop bag on the back seat. At 9:15 a.m., the garage camera shows {D} break the rear window with a small hammer and take the bag. {V} returned at 4 p.m. to glass on the seat. A tracker in the bag led deputies to {D}'s car two days later. {D} says the bag was left on the pavement.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Garage Camera", "{D} breaks the rear window with a hammer and takes a bag at 9:15 a.m."), E(.digital, 3, "Bag Tracker", "The bag pings from {D}'s address two days later."), E(.physical, 2, "Hammer", "A small hammer with glass fragments found in {D}'s trunk."), E(.document, 2, "Repair Estimate", "$420 to replace the rear window.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Found on Pavement", "{DL} says the bag was lying on the pavement and {D.he} picked it up."), E(.document, 1, "Maintenance Note", "A work order for broken glass near the garage entrance.")],
        role: "Car owner",
        exam: [.direct("Where did you park on the morning of {DATE}?", "\"In a hospital parking garage, about 7:30 a.m. I was visiting a relative. I left a laptop bag on the back seat, which I normally would not do.\""), .direct("What did you find when you came back?", "\"At about four in the afternoon, I found the rear window smashed and glass all over the back seat. The laptop bag was gone.\""), .direct("What did the garage camera show?", "\"At 9:15 a.m., {D} walks up to my car with a small hammer, breaks the rear window, reaches in, and takes the bag, then walks off.\""), .direct("What was in the bag?", "\"My work laptop, a charger, a notebook, and some paperwork. I had a tracker in it because I'd lost a bag before.\""), .direct("What did the tracker show?", "\"Two days later, the bag pinged from a residential address, and deputies went there. They found {DL}'s car and a hammer in the trunk.\""), .direct("What did the window cost?", "\"$420 to replace the rear window. I have the estimate from the glass shop.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} take the bag?", "\"No. I was in the hospital. I saw it afterward on the camera, and I recognized my own bag.\""), .cross("Does the video show the defendant swing the hammer?", "\"It shows a motion at the window, and glass falls. The angle is not perfect, but it looks like {D.he} breaks it.\""), .cross("Were other windows broken in that garage that week?", "\"I heard about a few, but I don't know details. The deputies never compared them to mine.\""), .cross("Was there glass on the pavement before you parked?", "\"I did not notice any. I parked near the entrance, and I wasn't looking at the ground.\""), .cross("Did you leave the bag visible?", "\"Yes. It was on the back seat in plain view. I know I should have put it in the trunk.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Garage attendant",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your job at the garage?", "\"I'm a garage attendant. I walk the levels, check on customers, and report maintenance issues to the office.\""), .direct("Were you working on {DATE}?", "\"Yes, from seven to three. I walk each level every couple of hours.\""), .direct("Do you recall broken glass that day?", "\"A work order was written for broken glass near the garage entrance. I remember a mess of glass there.\""), .direct("How often does glass get broken?", "\"More than we like. Windows have been smashed a few times, and we've had reports before.\""), .direct("Did you see {D} at the garage?", "\"I see so many people. I cannot say I noticed {D} specifically.\""), .direct("What did you do about the glass?", "\"I swept it up that afternoon. The office wrote a maintenance note about it.\""), .cross("Did you see anyone break a window at 9:15?", "\"No. I was on another level. I didn't see anything happen.\""), .cross("Do you know whose car had the broken window?", "\"Not that morning. I later learned it was a visitor.\""), .cross("Was the glass near the entrance from the car that was broken?", "\"I don't know. I did not check where the glass came from.\""), .cross("Did you see anyone carrying a bag?", "\"Dozens of people. I did not pay attention to any particular bag.\""), .cross("Would you leave a bag on the pavement?", "\"No. Nobody would leave a laptop bag lying around.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} smashed a window and took a bag.", "{D} picked up a bag from the pavement."),
        allocution: "\"I took what wasn't mine, and I'm sorry for it.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had smashed windows in the garage twice before that week.", "The bag was on the pavement because someone else had already broken the window."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why were you at the hospital garage that morning?", "\"I was heading into the hospital for an appointment. I park there often because it is close.\""), .direct("What did you see near the car?", "\"I saw a bag on the pavement near a car with a broken window. Glass was scattered all around it.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I picked up the bag. I figured someone had broken in and dropped it while running off, and I thought I would take it to security.\""), .direct("Why didn't you take it to security?", "\"I got distracted by my appointment, and then I took it home. I know how bad that sounds.\""), .direct("What about the hammer in your trunk?", "\"I keep a small hammer in the trunk for emergencies. It has been there for years, and the glass on it could be from anywhere.\""), .direct("What did you do with the bag?", "\"I left it in my living room and did not open it. I did not know about the tracker.\""), .cross("The camera shows you at the car at 9:15, doesn't it?", "\"It shows someone at the car. I was in the garage that morning. I did not break the window.\""), .cross("You took the bag home instead of turning it in, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I should have turned it in. I made a poor decision.\""), .cross("Your hammer had glass fragments on it, didn't it?", "\"I'm told so. I have been in several garages, and I've used the hammer for other things.\""), .cross("The tracker led deputies to your address, didn't it?", "\"It did. The bag was in my home, and I'm not denying that. I'm saying I picked it up.\""), .cross("You had been in that garage before that week, hadn't you?", "\"I park there regularly. I'm not going to say more than that.\"")],
        openings: ("At 9:15 a.m., the hospital garage camera shows {D} break a rear window with a small hammer and take a laptop bag from the back seat. Two days later, a tracker in the bag led deputies to {D}'s home, and a hammer with glass on it was in {D}'s trunk. The repair is $420.", "{D} says the bag was lying on the pavement near a car that had already been broken into, and {D} picked it up. A garage attendant will tell you broken glass was a recurring problem at that entrance. The State must prove {D} was the one who broke the window."),
        closings: ("Window, hammer, bag, on camera. Then a tracker pinging from {D}'s address and glass fragments in the trunk. {V} lost a laptop and a window.", "Glass breaks in that garage often, and no one has compared this window to the others that week. The hammer's fragments were never matched. A bag found at a home is not proof of who broke the glass."),
        timeline: [(0, "7:30 a.m.: {V} parks."), (0, "9:15 a.m.: {D} breaks the window."), (0, "4 p.m.: {V} finds the glass."), (2, "The tracker pings from {D}'s address.")],
        identified: "The garage camera identifies {D}.",
        notDone: ["Other windows broken that week were never compared.", "The hammer's glass fragments were never matched."],
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let chaseOnBikeV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.chaseOnBike",
        category: .traffic,
        headlines: ["Scooter Rider Speeds Away When Deputy Orders Stop at Night, Ditches Scooter in Creek", "Deputy Follows Moped Down Greenway Path Until It Is Dumped"],
        law: "fleeing",
        spec: "Operated a moped on a street while fleeing a law enforcement officer, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "At 10:45 p.m. on {DATE}, a deputy ordered {D} to stop a moped that had no taillight. {D} accelerated, rode through a church lot and onto a greenway path, and dumped the moped by a creek. The deputy lost sight of {D} for four minutes and found {D} hiding in brush at 10:55 p.m. {D} says {D.he} did not know it was a deputy.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Body Camera", "The deputy calls for the rider to stop and {D} accelerates at 10:46 p.m."), E(.document, 2, "Deputy's Report", "Lights and siren on from 10:46 p.m.; the chase ended at the creek."), E(.physical, 2, "Moped", "Found on its side by the creek, still warm, registered to {D}."), E(.statement, 2, "Church Neighbor", "Saw the moped cut through the lot with a cruiser behind it.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Did Not Know", "{DL} says {D.he} did not know it was a deputy."), E(.document, 1, "Weather Record", "Rain between 10 and 11 p.m. that night.")],
        role: "Sheriff's deputy",
        exam: [.direct("What were you doing at 10:45 p.m. on {DATE}?", "\"I was on patrol in a marked cruiser when I saw a moped with no taillight. I decided to make a traffic stop.\""), .direct("What did you do to initiate the stop?", "\"I activated my emergency lights and called out for the rider to stop. The body camera records it, and the rider looked back at me.\""), .direct("What did {D} do?", "\"At 10:46, {D} accelerated, cut through a church parking lot, and onto a greenway path. I followed with lights and siren.\""), .direct("How did the pursuit end?", "\"At about 10:51, {DL} dumped the moped by a creek and ran into brush. I lost sight of {DL} for four minutes.\""), .direct("How did you find the defendant?", "\"I searched the brush with a flashlight and found {DL} hiding at 10:55. The moped was on its side, still warm, and registered to {DL}.\""), .direct("Was anyone else a witness?", "\"A church neighbor told me the moped cut through the lot with a cruiser behind it, and I saw the neighbor's statement.\""), .cross("Was it raining that night?", "\"Yes, between ten and eleven. It was a steady rain, and it affected visibility.\""), .cross("Was your siren on when you first called for the stop?", "\"My lights were on first. The siren came on a moment later, after {D.he} accelerated.\""), .cross("Did the defendant speak to you when you found {D.him}?", "\"{DL} said {D.he} was scared and did not realize I was a deputy. I did not argue the point.\""), .cross("How far were you behind the defendant on the road?", "\"Perhaps thirty yards at the start, growing at times. I could see the tail of the moped but not much else.\""), .cross("Did the church lot camera show the distance?", "\"I did not review it. It could show how close I was.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Greenway jogger",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Where were you that night?", "\"I was jogging on the greenway near the creek when the rain started. I was heading back to my car.\""), .direct("What did you see and hear?", "\"A moped came flying down the path, followed by a cruiser's lights and siren. It was loud, and I stepped off the path.\""), .direct("Was the siren clear?", "\"Not very. The rain was loud on the leaves, and the sound seemed to come and go.\""), .direct("What did the rider do?", "\"The rider swerved and then dropped the moped by the creek. I saw someone run into the brush.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I stayed back and watched. A deputy came running, and I pointed to where the person went.\""), .direct("Could the rider have thought it was an ambulance?", "\"It sounded like some kind of siren. In the rain, I could have thought the same.\""), .cross("Did you see the rider's face?", "\"No. It was dark and wet, and the rider wore a hood.\""), .cross("Did you see the cruiser's lights?", "\"Yes, flashing blue and red. They were bright.\""), .cross("How far were you from the creek?", "\"About fifty feet, off the path.\""), .cross("Did you hear the deputy give commands?", "\"I heard shouting but not words. The rain made it hard.\""), .cross("Do you know {D}?", "\"No. I'd never seen {D} before.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} fled on a moped from a deputy.", "{D} did not know it was a deputy."),
        allocution: "\"I'm lucky no one was hurt, and I know it.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} looked back twice at the cruiser's lights.", "The rain muffled the siren and {DL} thought it was an ambulance."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why were you on the moped that night?", "\"I was riding home from a friend's place. The moped has a weak light, which I knew I needed to fix.\""), .direct("What did you notice behind you?", "\"Lights, and some noise. It was raining, and I thought it was an ambulance or a fire truck.\""), .direct("Why did you speed up?", "\"I was trying to get out of the way. I didn't want to be in the lane of an emergency vehicle.\""), .direct("Why did you cut through the church lot?", "\"It was a shortcut I use to get off the main road. I thought the vehicle would pass.\""), .direct("Why did you dump the moped?", "\"Fear. I realized it was following me, and I couldn't see well in the rain. I panicked and jumped off.\""), .direct("What did you do once you realized it was a deputy?", "\"I stayed down in the brush, shaking. When the deputy came, I did not run.\""), .cross("You looked back at the cruiser twice, didn't you?", "\"I looked back, yes. I saw lights. I still thought it was a different kind of vehicle.\""), .cross("You kept going on the greenway after that, didn't you?", "\"I did. I should have stopped. I was frightened and not thinking.\""), .cross("Your moped was still warm when found, wasn't it?", "\"It would be, I rode it hard.\""), .cross("You hid in the brush for four minutes, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I was afraid to come out.\""), .cross("The cruiser's lights are bright, aren't they?", "\"They are. I'm not saying I could not see them. I'm saying I did not know what they meant.\"")],
        openings: ("A deputy lit up a moped with no taillight at 10:45. {D} accelerated through a church lot, onto a greenway, and dumped the moped by a creek before hiding in the brush. The body camera shows the rider looking back at the lights.", "It was raining hard, the siren came and went, and {D} thought an ambulance was behind {D.him}. {D} never fought or lied, and stayed in the brush until found. You will hear from a jogger who also struggled to tell what that siren was."),
        closings: ("Lights, a siren, a look over the shoulder, and a moped thrown down by a creek. {D} fled for six minutes and hid. A person who is simply scared pulls over.", "In heavy rain, a muffled siren, and a deputy with a cruiser thirty yards behind, {D} did not know it was law enforcement. The siren's audibility was never tested and the church lot camera was never reviewed. The State must prove {D} knew."),
        timeline: [(0, "10:45 p.m.: the deputy orders the stop."), (0, "10:46 p.m.: {D} accelerates."), (0, "10:51 p.m.: the moped is dumped."), (0, "10:55 p.m.: deputies find {D} in the brush.")],
        identified: "The moped is registered to {D}.",
        notDone: ["The siren's audibility in the rain was never tested.", "The church lot camera was never reviewed for the cruiser's distance."],
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let cardSwapGasV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.cardSwapGas",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Shopper Uses Skimmed Card at Self-Checkout for $240 in Groceries", "Receipt and Bank Flag Tie Card to Skimming Case"],
        law: "cardFraud",
        spec: "Obtained groceries valued at $240 from {V}, a grocery store, by fraudulent card use, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "At 4:20 p.m. on {DATE}, {D} used a card at a self-checkout lane for $240 in groceries and a gift card. The bank flagged the card as cloned the next morning. The store camera shows {D} swipe three different cards before one worked. {D} says the card was found in the parking lot and {D.he} meant to turn it in.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Self-Checkout Camera", "{D} swipes three cards before one is approved at 4:22 p.m."), E(.document, 3, "Bank Notice", "The approved card was cloned and reported the next morning."), E(.document, 2, "Receipt", "$240 in groceries and a $50 gift card."), E(.physical, 2, "Cards", "Four other cards found in {D}'s wallet.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Found in Lot", "{DL} says {D.he} found the card in the lot and meant to turn it in."), E(.document, 1, "Lost Card Note", "A note on a receipt: 'found card, turn in.'")],
        role: "Store security officer",
        exam: [.direct("What do you do for the store, and what is your connection to this case?", "\"I'm a store security officer. The morning after {DATE}, the bank flagged a card used at our self-checkout, and I pulled the camera footage for the lane.\""), .direct("When did the transaction take place?", "\"{D} started at self-checkout around 4:20 p.m. and finished at 4:22. The total was $240 in groceries plus a $50 gift card.\""), .direct("What does the footage show about the cards?", "\"{DL} swipes three different cards in a row. The first two are declined, and the third goes through at 4:22. {DL} then bags everything and leaves.\""), .direct("What did the bank report?", "\"The approved card had been cloned, and the real cardholder reported it the next morning. The bank sent us a notice with the transaction time.\""), .direct("What did deputies find on {D}?", "\"Four other cards in {D.his} wallet. I wasn't present for the search, but I saw the property list the deputy wrote.\""), .direct("What was bought?", "\"Groceries, mostly packaged food and household items, and a fifty-dollar gift card. The receipt itemizes it all.\""), .cross("Did you see the defendant on the lot before entering?", "\"No. Our parking lot camera was not part of what I pulled. I can't say where {D.he} came from.\""), .cross("Did the lane flag anything at the time?", "\"The lane showed two declines, which is common when a customer fumbles with cards. No alarm went off.\""), .cross("Were the four other cards in the defendant's wallet cloned?", "\"I don't know. The owners were never contacted, and no one has told me those cards were bad.\""), .cross("Did the defendant try to hide the cards from the camera?", "\"No. {DL} handled them in plain view and did not cover the keypad. It looked like someone trying cards one after another.\""), .cross("Did the defendant ask an attendant for help?", "\"I don't see that on the video. An attendant was at the next lane, but {D.he} never waved for assistance.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Cashier at the next lane",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What do you do at the store?", "\"I'm a cashier. On {DATE} I was staffing the lane next to the self-checkout, where I help customers who get stuck.\""), .direct("Do you remember {D}?", "\"I recall a customer at the self-checkout struggling with cards. {D} looked flustered, like someone who couldn't get a payment to work.\""), .direct("How many cards did the defendant try?", "\"Several. I saw at least two declines before it went through. I did not count, because I was ringing someone up.\""), .direct("Did the defendant ask you for help?", "\"No. If a card declines more than once, a screen asks the customer to call an attendant. {D.He} did not do that.\""), .direct("What is typical for customers who have trouble paying?", "\"Most fiddle with cards, try a second one, or ask for help. Some get embarrassed and leave. It happens every day.\""), .direct("Did the defendant say anything about a found card?", "\"Not to me. I did not talk to {D.him} at all that afternoon.\""), .cross("Did you see whose card the defendant used?", "\"No. I could not see names, only the screen and the swipes.\""), .cross("Do you know whether any card was cloned?", "\"No. I only learned later that the bank flagged one.\""), .cross("Is it normal for a person to try three cards?", "\"Three is on the high side. People with a card problem might try two. I'd say three made me notice.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} look around?", "\"I wasn't watching for that. I was working my own lane.\""), .cross("Did the defendant pass the service desk?", "\"The desk is by the exit. I think {D.he} walked by it, but I did not see where {D.he} looked.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} used a cloned card for groceries.", "{D} found a card and meant to return it."),
        allocution: "\"I knew better. I want to make it right.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had been using cloned cards for weeks.", "{DL} did find one card and tried the others by mistake."),
        defendant: [.direct("Where did you get the first card?", "\"I found it in the parking lot, lying near the cart return. It looked like someone had dropped it. I picked it up with the idea of turning it in.\""), .direct("Why did you go into the store with it?", "\"I was already shopping, and I meant to hand it to a cashier. I put it in my pocket, and then the self-checkout line pulled me in.\""), .direct("Why did you try it at the self-checkout?", "\"I should not have. I was testing whether it was live so I'd know what to tell the store. It was stupid, and I knew it was wrong while I was doing it.\""), .direct("Why did you swipe three cards?", "\"Two of the cards were my own, and they were having problems. The third was the one I found. I swiped them one after another without thinking.\""), .direct("What did you plan to do with the found card?", "\"Give it to the service desk on my way out. I wrote a note on a receipt that said found card, turn in.\""), .direct("What happened when deputies stopped you?", "\"I told them right away where the card had come from. I did not argue. I told them about the note.\""), .cross("The third card was approved and you walked out with the groceries, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It went through and I took the bags. I'm not going to deny I left with $240 of food.\""), .cross("You didn't stop at the service desk, did you?", "\"No. I walked past it. I told myself I'd do it after, and I didn't.\""), .cross("You had four other cards in your wallet, didn't you?", "\"I had several cards, yes. A lot of people do. I have no explanation beyond that for each one.\""), .cross("You bought a $50 gift card with it, didn't you?", "\"Yes, on the same transaction. It's hard to explain that as accidental.\""), .cross("Your note on the receipt was written after the purchase, wasn't it?", "\"I wrote it later that afternoon. I can't say it was before. I understand how that looks.\"")],
        openings: ("At 4:20 p.m., {D} swiped three cards at the self-checkout until the third was approved for $240 in groceries and a $50 gift card. The bank flagged that card as cloned the next morning, and four more cards were in {D}'s wallet. The self-checkout camera shows every swipe.", "{D} says one card was found in the parking lot and a receipt note shows the plan to turn it in. Two other cards in the wallet were {D}'s own and were failing. You will hear from a cashier who saw a flustered customer, not a skilled thief."),
        closings: ("Three cards, one approval, and groceries out the door. The approved card was cloned, and a gift card was added to the order. A person who truly meant to turn in a card would not buy groceries with it.", "A card found on the pavement, a note about turning it in, and two cards of {D}'s own that were failing. The parking lot camera was never checked and the owners of the other cards were never contacted. The State must prove {D} knew the card was not {D.his}."),
        timeline: [(0, "4:20 p.m.: {D} starts the self-checkout."), (0, "4:22 p.m.: the third card is approved."), (1, "The bank flags the card."), (2, "The store sends the camera video.")],
        identified: "The self-checkout camera identifies {D}.",
        notDone: ["The parking lot camera was never checked for where {DL} found the card.", "The other cards' owners were never contacted."],
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let passwordBorrowV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.passwordBorrow",
        category: .cyber,
        headlines: ["Former Coworker Posts From Colleague's Social Account Using Saved Login on Shared Laptop", "Account Log Shows Login From Office Network After Resignation"],
        law: "accessingComputers",
        spec: "Willfully accessed the computer account of {V} without authority, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} left a job and returned to the office on {DATE} to pick up belongings. {D} used a shared laptop on which {V}'s social media account was still logged in and posted three messages under {V}'s name. {V} was locked out and asked the platform for the login history, which showed the office network and the time of the posts. {D} says the laptop was left logged in.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Account Login History", "Three posts from the office network at 4:10 p.m. under {V}'s account."), E(.digital, 3, "Post Contents", "Three messages insulting a client posted under {V}'s name."), E(.document, 2, "Visitor Badge Log", "{D} signed in at 3:55 p.m. and out at 4:30 p.m."), E(.statement, 2, "{V}", "Never logged in or posted those messages.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Left Logged In", "{DL} says the laptop was left logged in and {D.he} did not know whose it was."), E(.document, 1, "Laptop Photo", "A photo of the shared laptop with a sticky note.")],
        role: "Account owner",
        exam: [.direct("What happened to your social media account?", "\"Three messages insulting a client were posted under my name at 4:10 p.m. I did not write them.\""), .direct("What did the login history show?", "\"The posts came from the office network. The platform showed the time and location of each post.\""), .direct("How was {D} connected to this?", "\"{D} had left the job and came to the office that day to pick up belongings. The visitor badge log shows {DL} in from 3:55 to 4:30.\""), .direct("What happened with your account?", "\"I was locked out at about 4:30, and then I saw three insulting messages about a client posted under my name. I had never written them.\""), .direct("How did you trace the posts?", "\"I asked the platform for the login history. It showed three posts from the office network at 4:10 p.m.\""), .direct("Who was in the office then?", "\"{DL}, a former colleague, had signed in at 3:55 to pick up belongings. {DL} signed out at 4:30.\""), .cross("{D} says the laptop was left logged in, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"The laptop was shared, and I was usually logged in on it. I agree with that.\""), .cross("Did you tell {D} not to use it?", "\"No. I was not there. I only learned later.\""), .cross("Did the defendant threaten you at the exit interview?", "\"I heard {DL} said something about making me look bad. I did not hear it myself.\""), .cross("You left your account logged in on the shared laptop, didn't you?", "\"I used the laptop that morning and probably did not log out. That was careless.\""), .cross("The laptop had a sticky note on it, didn't it?", "\"Yes, a note with a password hint for the office account. It did not name mine.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Office manager",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Was the laptop shared among your team?", "\"By the whole team. Everyone used it for quick tasks, and nobody kept their own login on it.\""), .direct("Was {V} usually logged in on the shared laptop?", "\"Usually. {V} liked to stay logged in so the posts would be handy for the team.\""), .direct("Did {D} ask permission before using it?", "\"I do not recall. {D} may have asked someone, but I do not remember it being me.\""), .direct("What is your role?", "\"I manage the front office, and I handle badges and shared equipment. I signed {D.him} in that afternoon.\""), .direct("What was the laptop situation?", "\"A shared laptop used by several people. Whoever used it last often left things open.\""), .direct("What did you see?", "\"{D.He} used the laptop for about ten minutes. I was on the phone and did not look.\""), .cross("Did the defendant still have a badge when the posts were made?", "\"The badge was returned that day, I believe. {D.He} signed in as a visitor.\""), .cross("Would a former employee normally use a shared laptop?", "\"Not normally. {D.He} should have stayed away from it.\""), .cross("Did you see the defendant post anything?", "\"No. I did not see that. I only know about the laptop.\""), .cross("You did not see what the defendant typed, did you?", "\"No. I was working at my desk.\""), .cross("The account was {V}'s, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I did not know whose it was until later.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} used a logged-in laptop to post as {V}.", "{D} did not know the account was {V}'s."),
        allocution: "\"I didn't think about what it would do to the person on the other end.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had threatened to 'make {V} look bad' at the exit interview.", "{DL} thought the laptop was the office's account."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you post the three messages under {V}'s name?", "\"I used the shared laptop, and the account was logged in. I thought it was the office's account.\""), .direct("Why did you post on the laptop?", "\"I was angry about leaving the job. I typed some messages without thinking about whose account it was.\""), .direct("Was the laptop left logged in?", "\"Yes. It was open and logged in. I did not log in myself.\""), .direct("Why did you return to the office?", "\"To collect my box of belongings and a few files. I was told to sign in at the front.\""), .direct("What did you do on the laptop?", "\"I opened the laptop to look something up, and a social media page was open. I posted three messages without looking at whose account it was.\""), .direct("What did you think about the account?", "\"I thought it was the office account because the laptop was shared. I did not see the name.\""), .cross("The messages insulted a client under {V}'s name, didn't they?", "\"Yes. I know that. It was wrong.\""), .cross("You thought the account belonged to the office. Why post insults there?", "\"I was not thinking. I wanted to vent.\""), .cross("You said at your exit interview you would make {V} look bad, didn't you?", "\"I said something like that in anger. I did not mean to do it.\""), .cross("The messages insulted a client, didn't they?", "\"Yes. I was upset, and I wrote what I felt.\""), .cross("You said at the exit interview that you would make {V} look bad, didn't you?", "\"I said something like that in anger. It was not a plan, and I regret saying it.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} left a job and returned to the office to pick up belongings. Using a shared laptop on which {V}'s social media account was still logged in, three messages insulting a client were posted under {V}'s name at 4:10 p.m.", "The defense case is that the laptop was shared, that the account was left logged in, and that {D} believed it was the office's account."),
        closings: ("Three insulting posts under {V}'s name from the office network while {D} was signed in as a visitor. {D} had threatened to make {V} look bad.", "A shared laptop, an account left logged in, and a confused former employee. The State must prove {D} knew the account was {V}'s."),
        timeline: [(0, "3:55 p.m.: {D} signs in."), (0, "4:10 p.m.: the posts are made."), (0, "4:30 p.m.: {D} signs out."), (1, "{V} asks the platform for the login history.")],
        identified: "The account log traces to {D}'s visit.",
