        openings: ("{V} set a phone and wallet worth $520 on a laundromat table, and at 7:17 {D}, folding at the next table, put both into a laundry bag. The phone later pinged from {D}'s address, and a card from the wallet was used that night.", "Jurors will hear that the two phones were the same model, that {D} picked up the wrong one at a crowded laundromat, and never meant to take {V}'s things."),
