        openings: ("At 5:20 p.m., {D} took two bottles of wine worth $52 from a grocery shelf, tucked them under a jacket, and walked to the exit. A loss prevention officer stopped {D} without a receipt.", "The defense case is that {D} had cash, meant to pay at the register, and treated it as a joke that went too far."),
