        exam: [.direct("What happened at the bus stop at 8 p.m.?", "\"I was waiting for the bus when an airsoft pellet struck my thigh. It left a welt.\""), .direct("What does the doorbell camera across the street show?", "\"{D} on a porch with a pistol at 8:01, firing toward the bus stop.\""), .direct("What was recovered?", "\"A plastic pellet at the bus stop. I called deputies at 8:10.\""), .direct("What were you doing at 8 p.m.?", "\"Standing at the bus stop after work, looking at my phone and waiting for the number 12. It was dusk and the street was quiet.\""), .direct("What did you feel and see?", "\"A sharp sting on my thigh, like a hard flick, and a small plastic pellet bounced on the pavement. I looked across the street and saw someone on a porch with a pistol.\""), .direct("What did you do afterward?", "\"I picked up the pellet, took a photo of the porch, and called deputies at 8:10. By the next day I had a welt the size of a half dollar.\""), .cross("{D} says {D.he} was shooting at a can and you wandered into the line, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"A can was on the rail. I did not walk into any line. I was waiting at the stop.\""), .cross("How far is the porch from the bus stop?", "\"Across the street. It is some distance.\""), .cross("Did the defendant aim at you?", "\"I cannot say. I know I was hit.\""), .cross("You did not see the defendant aim at you, did you?", "\"I saw the pistol pointed in my direction, but I cannot say whether the aim was at me or at something near me.\""), .cross("The bus stop was in line with the porch, wasn't it?", "\"Yes, directly across the street. A can on the porch rail would be in line with the stop too.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Porch neighbor",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did you hear the shot from the porch across the street?", "\"A pop. It was a small sound, like a cap gun, and I almost did not notice it over the traffic.\""), .direct("Did you see who fired the shot from across the street?", "\"From across the street, I saw someone on the porch with a pistol raised toward the road.\""), .direct("Was {D} aiming at the bus stop when you saw {D.him}?", "\"I cannot say. I only saw the person raise the pistol, and I could not tell where it was pointed.\""), .direct("Where do you live in relation to the defendant?", "\"On the same street, a few doors down, with a clear view of {D}'s porch. I was sitting outside that evening.\""), .direct("What did you see the defendant doing?", "\"Shooting a pistol at a can on the porch rail, several times over about ten minutes. It looked like target practice.\""), .direct("What did you hear after the shots?", "\"A yell from the bus stop, then silence. {D.He} looked up and put the pistol down quickly.\""), .cross("Was the porch light on when you saw the person?", "\"Yes. It was lit, and I could see the porch well enough to know it was {D.his} house.\""), .cross("Had the defendant shot at things from that porch before?", "\"Once or twice. I heard pops from that porch before, but I never saw what was being shot.\""), .cross("Was a can sitting on the porch rail that evening?", "\"I think so. I saw something on the rail, though it was small and I could not tell what.\""), .cross("You did not see where the pellets went, did you?", "\"No. I only saw the can and {D.his} arm. I cannot say where each pellet landed.\""), .cross("A bus stop across the street is in the line of fire, isn't it?", "\"In a straight line, yes. I had not thought about that before this.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} shot a pedestrian from a porch.", "{D} was aiming at a can."),
        allocution: "\"I hurt someone who didn't deserve it. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had shot at passing cars the week before.", "A can was on the rail and {V} was in the line of fire."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you shoot {V}?", "\"I shot at a can on my rail. I did not see {V.him}. The pellet went where I did not intend.\""), .direct("Why were you shooting from the porch?", "\"For fun. I was plinking at a can with an airsoft pistol.\""), .direct("Did you see anyone at the bus stop?", "\"No. I did not see anyone. I did not look at the stop.\""), .direct("What were you shooting at?", "\"A soda can balanced on the porch rail, with an airsoft pistol I own for target practice. I shoot cans at dusk when it is quiet.\""), .direct("What happened that evening?", "\"I fired a few rounds at the can, and one went wide. I saw someone grab a leg across the street and realized the pellet had traveled farther than I expected.\""), .direct("What did you do then?", "\"I put the pistol down and went inside, then waited for deputies. I felt terrible, and I did not intend to hit anyone.\""), .cross("A bus stop is across the street. Why shoot in that direction?", "\"The can was in line with it. I should have thought.\""), .cross("{V} was hit in the thigh. Do you accept that?", "\"Yes. I apologize.\""), .cross("You had shot toward passing cars the week before, hadn't you?", "\"Yes, a couple of times, which I now regret. I thought the pellets were harmless at that range.\""), .cross("You fired toward a public bus stop, didn't you?", "\"The can was in front of it, and I fired in that direction without checking who was there. That was careless.\""), .cross("The bus stop is across the street, so anything you shot toward the can went toward it, didn't it?", "\"The can was on the rail, and I did not think anyone was in the line. I should have looked before I pulled the trigger.\"")],
        openings: ("At 8 p.m., {V} was waiting at a bus stop when an airsoft pellet struck {V} in the thigh. A doorbell camera across the street shows {D} on a porch with a pistol, firing toward the stop.", "Jurors will hear that {D} was shooting at a can on the porch rail and that {V} was struck by a stray pellet in the line of fire."),
        closings: ("A pistol on a porch, a shot toward a bus stop, and a welt on {V}'s thigh. {D} had shot at passing cars the week before.", "A can on a rail and a pellet that went astray. The State must prove {D} fired at {V} or knew {V} was in the line of fire."),
        timeline: [(0, "8 p.m.: {V} waits at the stop."), (0, "8:01 p.m.: the pellet hits."), (0, "8:10 p.m.: {V} calls deputies."), (1, "{V} sees a doctor.")],
        identified: "The doorbell camera identifies {D}.",
        notDone: ["The pistol's muzzle velocity was never tested.", "The welt was never photographed on the first day."],
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let snowballCarV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.snowballCar",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Rock Thrown From Hillside at Passing Delivery Truck Cracks Windshield", "Hillside Camera Shows Throw and Delivery Van Stopping"],
        law: "injuryPersonalProperty",
        spec: "Willfully and wantonly injured personal property of {V}, a delivery truck, causing damage of $620, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "At 3:20 p.m. on {DATE}, {D} threw a fist-sized rock from a grassy hillside beside a road at a passing delivery truck. The rock struck the windshield and cracked it from edge to edge. The driver stopped and called deputies at 3:25 p.m. A hillside camera recorded the throw. The windshield cost $620 to replace. {D} says {D.he} was aiming at a sign.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Hillside Camera", "{D} throws a rock at the truck at 3:20 p.m."), E(.physical, 2, "Rock", "A fist-sized rock on the truck's hood."), E(.document, 2, "Repair Invoice", "$620 to replace the windshield."), E(.statement, 2, "{V}", "The rock struck as {V} was driving past.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Aiming at a Sign", "{DL} says {D.he} was aiming at a road sign and the truck passed."), E(.document, 1, "Road Sign Photo", "A photo of a sign eighty feet down the hill with a fresh dent.")],
        role: "Delivery truck driver",
        exam: [.direct("What did your delivery truck show?", "\"The rock landed on the hood. I stopped and called deputies at 3:25.\""), .direct("What happened on the road?", "\"At 3:20 I was driving a delivery truck down a county road beside a grassy hillside when a rock came out of nowhere and struck the windshield. The glass cracked edge to edge.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I braked, pulled onto the shoulder, and called deputies at 3:25. The rock sat on the hood, about the size of my fist.\""), .direct("What did the hillside camera show?", "\"It shows {D} standing on the slope, winding up, and throwing the rock toward the road as my truck passed. It happened in about two seconds.\""), .direct("What did you do when the windshield cracked?", "\"I held the wheel steady, slowed down and pulled onto the shoulder. I checked myself for glass and then called 911.\""), .direct("What happened to your route that day because of the windshield?", "\"I had to leave the truck at the shoulder and wait for a tow. The rest of my deliveries were reassigned to another driver.\""), .cross("{D} says {D.he} was aiming at a sign, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"A sign nearby was dented by an earlier rock. I will give you that.\""), .cross("Did you see the defendant?", "\"I saw a person on the grass. I could not make out a face.\""), .cross("Were you hurt?", "\"No. The glass held. I was shaken.\""), .cross("There is a road sign down the hill, isn't there?", "\"Yes, about eighty feet from where {D.he} stood. It has a fresh dent in a photo.\""), .cross("You did not see the defendant before the rock came, did you?", "\"No. I was watching the road and only saw the rock when it hit.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Hillside hiker",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did you see someone throw a rock from the hillside?", "\"A rock, yes. I saw it leave the hand of a person on the grass and head toward the road.\""), .direct("Who threw the rock that struck the truck?", "\"A person on the grass. I could not see the face from where I was standing on the trail.\""), .direct("Was the rock aimed at the truck, as far as you could tell?", "\"I could not tell. It went toward the road, and the truck was passing just then.\""), .direct("What were you doing on the hill?", "\"Hiking with a friend along the slope that afternoon. We paused to take photos of the view.\""), .direct("What did you see {D} do?", "\"{D} threw a rock toward the sign. A truck passed at the same moment, and the rock hit it.\""), .direct("How did the defendant react?", "\"{D.He} looked shocked and stood still. {D.He} did not try to leave.\""), .cross("Did the truck stop right after the rock hit?", "\"Right away. The driver pulled over and got out to look at the windshield.\""), .cross("Did you see the person throw more than one rock that day?", "\"I saw one. I did not see more, and I only noticed because of the crash on the windshield.\""), .cross("Was the sign near the road close to where the truck passed?", "\"Yes. It was close to where the truck passed, and it was easy to see how someone could miss.\""), .cross("You did not see the defendant aim at the truck, did you?", "\"No. I saw the throw but not the aim.\""), .cross("The truck was very close to the sign, wasn't it?", "\"It was passing near it, yes. It looked like an accident.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} threw a rock at a moving truck.", "{D} was aiming at a sign."),
        allocution: "\"I wasn't thinking about the person on the other end. I am now.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had thrown rocks at passing trucks the week before.", "The sign was dented by a different rock earlier."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you throw the rock at the delivery truck?", "\"I threw a rock at a sign by the road. The truck passed at the wrong moment, and I did not mean to hit it.\""), .direct("Why were you throwing rocks from the hillside?", "\"I was bored on the hillside. I was throwing at a sign as a game, with no one else around.\""), .direct("Had you thrown rocks at trucks on that road before?", "\"Not at trucks. I threw at signs. I did not mean to hit a truck, and I never aimed at one.\""), .direct("What were you doing on the hillside?", "\"Hiking and throwing rocks at a road sign down the slope for fun. I have done it a few times.\""), .direct("What happened with the truck?", "\"I threw at the sign just as a truck came through, and the rock sailed right into its path. I did not see it coming.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I froze, then stayed where I was when the driver stopped. I did not run.\""), .cross("You threw rocks at passing trucks the week before, didn't you?", "\"I threw rocks near the road. I did not aim at trucks, and I never meant to hit one.\""), .cross("The sign was dented by an earlier rock. Was that rock yours?", "\"Probably. I kept hitting that sign, and I guess I dented it. It was a game to me.\""), .cross("A new windshield cost $620. Will you pay that cost?", "\"Yes. I will pay for it. I am sorry about the damage and the fright I caused the driver.\""), .cross("The sign had been dented earlier by a different rock, hadn't it?", "\"Yes, a rock I threw before. It does not change what happened this time.\""), .cross("You threw more than one rock that afternoon, didn't you?", "\"I threw two or three. I was bored and angry about something else, and I did not think about who was driving.\"")],
        openings: ("At 3:20 p.m., {D} threw a fist-sized rock from a hillside at a passing delivery truck, cracking the windshield from edge to edge. A hillside camera recorded the throw, and the windshield cost $620.", "The defense evidence will establish that {D} was throwing at a sign near the road and that the truck passed at the wrong moment."),
        closings: ("A rock thrown from a hillside, a cracked windshield, and a camera that shows the throw. A driver was inches from serious harm.", "A game of throwing at a sign and a truck that passed at the wrong moment. The State must prove {D} aimed at the truck."),
        timeline: [(0, "3:20 p.m.: {D} throws the rock."), (0, "3:21 p.m.: the windshield cracks."), (0, "3:25 p.m.: the driver calls deputies."), (1, "The county sends the hillside video.")],
        identified: "The hillside camera identifies {D}.",
        notDone: ["The rock was never recovered from the road.", "The windshield's impact angle was never studied."],
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let sprinklerFightV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.sprinklerFight",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Argument Over Trash Bins at Curb Ends With Shove Into Recycling Cart", "Neighbor Camera Shows Shove and Cart Tipping"],
        law: "simpleAssault",
        spec: "Assaulted {V} by shoving {V.him}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "On {DATE} at 7 a.m., {D} and {V} argued at the curb over where {V} had put a recycling cart on trash day. {D} said the cart blocked {D}'s driveway and shoved {V} into it. The cart tipped and {V} bruised a hip and scraped an elbow. A neighbor's camera recorded the shove at 7:04 a.m. {D} says {V} stepped toward {D.him} with a raised fist.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Neighbor Camera", "{D} shoves {V} into the cart at 7:04 a.m."), E(.document, 2, "Medical Note", "A bruised hip and a scraped elbow."), E(.statement, 2, "Neighbor", "Saw the argument and the shove from a window."), E(.physical, 1, "Recycling Cart", "A cracked cart with a bent wheel.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Raised Fist", "{DL} says {V} stepped toward {D.him} with a raised fist."), E(.document, 1, "Photo of Driveway", "A photo of the cart six inches into {D}'s driveway.")],
        role: "Neighbor",
        exam: [.direct("What did you see at the curb on trash day?", "\"{D} and {V} argued over where {V} had put a recycling cart. Then {DL} shoved {V} into the cart at 7:04.\""), .direct("What was the result of the shove?", "\"The cart tipped. {V} bruised a hip and scraped an elbow, and the cart was cracked with a bent wheel.\""), .direct("What did your camera record?", "\"The whole shove. I also watched the argument from my window.\""), .direct("What was the argument about?", "\"Where I had put my recycling cart on trash day. {D.He} said it blocked the driveway apron, and I said it was on the curb where the city told us to place it.\""), .direct("What did {D} do?", "\"{D.He} stepped up and shoved me into the cart. It tipped, and I fell against it and hit my hip.\""), .direct("What were your injuries?", "\"A bruised hip and a scraped elbow. The cart cracked and one wheel bent.\""), .cross("{D} says {V} stepped toward {D.him} with a raised fist, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"I saw {V} raise a hand to point at the driveway. I did not see a fist.\""), .cross("Was the cart in {D}'s driveway?", "\"Partly. It was partly in the way.\""), .cross("Did the defendant apologize?", "\"No. {D.He} did not apologize.\""), .cross("The cart was partly in the defendant's driveway, wasn't it?", "\"A photo shows it six inches into the driveway. I did not think that was a big deal.\""), .cross("You raised a hand to point at the driveway, didn't you?", "\"Yes, to point at the line. I did not make a fist.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Other neighbor",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Was the recycling cart in {D}'s driveway?", "\"Partly. It sat across the edge of the apron, so a car could not easily get in.\""), .direct("Did you see the shove?", "\"From a window, yes. I saw {D} shove {V}, and the cart tipped over.\""), .direct("Did {V} yell at the defendant?", "\"Some. Both of them were raising their voices, and it was a loud argument over the cart.\""), .direct("How do you know about the argument?", "\"I live next door and heard raised voices while I was making coffee. I watched from my kitchen window.\""), .direct("What did you see?", "\"{DF} and {V} arguing at the curb, with {V} pointing at the driveway. Then {DF} shoved {V} into the cart.\""), .direct("How did it end?", "\"{V} fell and got up slowly, and {DF} walked inside. I called {V} to see if help was needed.\""), .cross("Did the defendant apologize afterward?", "\"No. I did not see {DF} apologize. {DF} walked away.\""), .cross("Had the defendant moved the cart before the shove?", "\"I heard that {D.he} had moved it three times before that morning.\""), .cross("Did {V} raise a hand toward the defendant?", "\"A hand to point at the driveway. I would not call it a punch.\""), .cross("You did not see {V} raise a fist, did you?", "\"I saw a raised hand, pointing. I did not see a fist.\""), .cross("The shove was clear on camera, wasn't it?", "\"Yes, and I saw it too.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} shoved {V} into a cart over trash day.", "{V} raised a fist."),
        allocution: "\"I'm not proud of it, Your Honor.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had moved the cart three times before the shove.", "{V} did raise a hand to point at the driveway."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you shove {V}?", "\"Yes. {V} stepped toward me with a raised hand, and I pushed {V.him} away. I did not mean for the cart to tip.\""), .direct("Why were you so upset about the cart?", "\"It blocked my driveway, and I had moved it three times. I was tired of it.\""), .direct("Did you apologize?", "\"No. I did not. I was still angry. That is on me.\""), .direct("How many times had the cart been in your way?", "\"Three mornings, and I had moved it each time myself. That morning I came out and it was there again.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I confronted {V} and we argued for a few minutes. When {V} stepped toward me with a raised hand, I shoved.\""), .direct("How has this affected you?", "\"I wish I had walked away. I should have called the city instead.\""), .cross("{V} raised a hand to point at the driveway, didn't {V.he}?", "\"Maybe. It looked like a fist to me in the moment.\""), .cross("You moved the cart three times before the shove, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I was frustrated. I should have called the city.\""), .cross("{V} bruised a hip and scraped an elbow. Do you regret that?", "\"Yes. I am so sorry. I should have walked away.\""), .cross("You shoved {V} into the cart, didn't you?", "\"Yes, with both hands. {V} fell into it.\""), .cross("{V} did not touch you first, did {V.he}?", "\"No, but I thought {V.he} was about to.\"")],
        openings: ("On trash day at 7 a.m., {D} and {V} argued at the curb over a recycling cart, and {D} shoved {V} into it. The cart tipped, and {V} bruised a hip and scraped an elbow, with a neighbor's camera recording it.", "By the end of this trial, the proof will show that the cart blocked {D}'s driveway, that {V} raised a hand toward {D}, and that {D} reacted in a moment of fear."),
        closings: ("A recycling cart, an argument at the curb, a shove on camera, and {V} injured. {D} moved the cart three times and then moved {V}, shoving a neighbor into it.", "A raised hand and a split-second shove after months of frustration. The State must prove {D} was not reacting to a perceived threat, and it has not."),
        timeline: [(0, "7 a.m.: {D} and {V} argue."), (0, "7:04 a.m.: the shove."), (0, "7:15 a.m.: {V} calls deputies."), (1, "The neighbor sends the camera video.")],
        identified: "The neighbor's camera identifies {D}.",
        notDone: ["The recycling cart's placement was never measured.", "The city's trash rules were never read into the record."],
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let bikeLaneShoveV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.bikeLaneShove",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Delivery E-Bike Rider Shoves Pedestrian Off Crosswalk Curb", "Intersection Camera Shows Shove After Light Changes"],
        law: "simpleAssault",
        spec: "Assaulted {V} by shoving {V.him} off a curb, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "At 6:40 p.m. on {DATE}, {D}, a delivery rider on an e-bike, ran a red light and nearly hit {V}, who was in a crosswalk. {V} shouted and {D} shoved {V} off the curb and rode away. {V} twisted an ankle in the gutter. An intersection camera recorded the shove at 6:41 p.m. {D} says {V} stepped out on a flashing hand.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Intersection Camera", "{D} shoves {V} off the curb at 6:41 p.m."), E(.document, 2, "Medical Note", "A twisted ankle and a scraped palm."), E(.statement, 2, "Bus Driver", "Saw the near miss and the shove from the stopped bus."), E(.digital, 2, "Delivery App Log", "{D}'s account shows an active delivery at 6:41 p.m.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Flashing Hand", "{DL} says {V} stepped out on a flashing hand."), E(.document, 1, "Signal Timing", "The signal chart shows a flashing hand for the last ten seconds of the light.")],
        role: "Bus driver",
        exam: [.direct("What route were you driving at 6:40 p.m. on {DATE}?", "\"I drive a city bus on the downtown loop. At that time I was stopped at a red light at a busy intersection, first in line, facing the crosswalk.\""), .direct("What did you see happen in the crosswalk?", "\"A pedestrian had started across when an e-bike came through the red light from my left, fast, and missed the pedestrian by what looked like a foot.\""), .direct("What did the pedestrian do?", "\"{V} shouted at the rider. I could see {V}'s mouth moving and an arm raised, though through the windshield I did not hear exact words.\""), .direct("What did the rider do?", "\"The rider swung the bike back toward the curb, put a hand out, and shoved {V} off the curb into the gutter. Then the rider pedaled off down the cross street.\""), .direct("What happened to {V}?", "\"{V} went down on one side in the gutter and grabbed an ankle. I set my brake, opened the door, and went to help while a passenger called out.\""), .direct("What did you do afterward?", "\"I called dispatch, and at 6:45 I called the police. I stayed with {V} until an officer came, and I gave my name as a witness.\""), .cross("What color was the pedestrian signal when {V} stepped out?", "\"I was watching the cross traffic and my own light, so I can't say what the walk signal showed when {V} left the curb.\""), .cross("Was the hand flashing at the time?", "\"I did not see it. The signal timing sheet says a flashing hand runs for ten seconds at the end of the light, but I never matched it to the moment.\""), .cross("How far were you from the corner?", "\"About thirty feet. I had a clear line of sight through the windshield, though a parked van was at the edge of my view.\""), .cross("Did {V} touch the bike or the rider before the shove?", "\"I did not see contact before the shove. {V} shouted and may have waved an arm, but I did not see a hand land.\""), .cross("Did you see how fast the e-bike was going?", "\"Fast, faster than a regular bike. Nobody recorded the actual speed, so all I can say is that it did not slow for the light.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Pedestrian waiting at the corner",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Where were you standing at 6:40 p.m. on {DATE}?", "\"On the corner, waiting to cross. I was at the front of a small group, about six feet from the curb, looking across at the signal.\""), .direct("What was the pedestrian signal showing?", "\"The hand had started flashing. I remember the countdown was in single digits when I saw someone step off the curb beside me.\""), .direct("Who stepped off?", "\"The person who later turned out to be {V}. {V} stepped into the crosswalk when the hand was already flashing, and I thought it was a risky time to start.\""), .direct("What did you see of the e-bike?", "\"It came through fast, from the left. It was close to {V}, and I jumped back from the curb.\""), .direct("What did you hear?", "\"Shouting, and then {V} falling. A bus was stopped nearby, and the driver came over.\""), .direct("How did the rider look?", "\"Rattled. The rider seemed to be reacting to {V} and was moving fast.\""), .cross("Did you see the shove?", "\"I saw an arm come out, and then {V} falling. I did not see the exact contact.\""), .cross("Did {V} step out after the hand started flashing?", "\"I believe so, but I was looking at the bike and not the signal the whole time. I can't give you a precise second.\""), .cross("Did the rider run a red light?", "\"The rider came through close to the red. I can't say whether it was yellow or red.\""), .cross("Did you stay and give a statement?", "\"Yes. I waited for the police and told them what I saw.\""), .cross("Do you know either person?", "\"No, neither. I was just standing on the corner.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} ran a light and shoved a pedestrian.", "{V} stepped out on a flashing hand."),
        allocution: "\"I'm not proud of it, Your Honor.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} shoved first without any contact from {V}.", "The hand was flashing and {V} had stepped out late."),
        defendant: [.direct("What were you doing on the e-bike that evening?", "\"I deliver food for an app, and I had an active order that I was trying to drop before the food went cold. It was the end of the dinner rush.\""), .direct("Did you run the red light?", "\"The light was yellow turning red when I entered. I thought I could clear it, and I probably went through a beat late.\""), .direct("What happened with the pedestrian?", "\"{V} stepped out into the crosswalk on a flashing hand, right in front of me. I braked and swerved, and {V} yelled at me.\""), .direct("Why did you shove {V}?", "\"I was scared and jumpy after nearly crashing. {V} came at me, and I pushed {V} away to protect myself. I did not mean to knock {V} off the curb.\""), .direct("Why did you ride away?", "\"I panicked and my order was late. I told myself I would call about it later. I know I should have stopped.\""), .direct("What would you say to {V}?", "\"That I am sorry about the ankle. I shouldn't have pushed anyone, and I should have stayed to help.\""), .cross("The camera shows you push {V} off the curb, doesn't it?", "\"It shows me pushing. I can't argue with that. I'm just telling you why I did it.\""), .cross("Your delivery app shows an active order at 6:41, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. I was on the clock and in a hurry. That is part of why I was moving fast.\""), .cross("A flashing hand means pedestrians should not start across, doesn't it?", "\"It means finish crossing if you started, and don't start. I believe {V} had started late.\""), .cross("You didn't stop after {V} fell, did you?", "\"No, I rode off. That is the worst part of what I did.\""), .cross("You didn't call anyone to report it, did you?", "\"No. I should have called and did not.\"")],
        openings: ("At 6:40 p.m., {D} ran a red light on an e-bike and nearly hit {V} in the crosswalk. When {V} shouted, {D} shoved {V} off the curb and rode away, leaving {V} with a twisted ankle. The intersection camera and a bus driver saw it.", "The hand was flashing when {V} stepped off the curb, and a delivery rider swerved to avoid a collision. {D} reacted in fear and was not trying to hurt anyone. You will hear from a pedestrian standing on the corner who saw the timing."),
        closings: ("A red light, a near miss, a shout, and then a shove on camera at 6:41. {V} ended up in the gutter with a twisted ankle and {D} rode off. The delivery app places {D} on the bike.", "A flashing hand, a bike coming fast, and a split second of fear. The signal timing was never matched to the video, and the e-bike's speed was never recorded. The State must prove {D} shoved {V} intentionally rather than reacting."),
