        openings: ("At a farmers market, {D} bought small items at three stalls with counterfeit tens. A produce vendor marked the first bill and security stopped {D} with four more in {D}'s pocket. You will see the bills and the black streaks the marker test left.", "{D} took out real cash the day before and got at least one of those tens as change at another stall. Bills circulate through a farmers market all morning, and a baker will tell you how easily a bad one travels. {D} was surprised when security stopped {D.him}."),
        closings: ("Seven counterfeit tens, three stalls, and a marker that streaked black each time. {D} spent them and had four more on hand. That is passing counterfeit money.", "A bad bill can pass through a dozen hands in a market morning, and {D} had an ATM receipt from the day before. The serial numbers were never traced to a bank. The State must prove {D} knew the bills were fake."),
